{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick","id":1492820,"title":"On Science and Magick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-11T12:42:37-07:00","id":1492820,"title":"On Science and Magick","content":"Is the Purple Paradigm True?<br /> <br /> From the beginning of Mage, there has been the notion that the truth of the setting is that reality is fundamentally subjective, that Magick is Enlightened Will altering reality, and that Science is Magick. It's so prevalent that it's unofficially been given the name \u201cthe Purple Paradigm\u201d (after the color of the core book). I don't buy it; not as an absolute, incontrovertible truth. <br /> <br /> It can and should be what the <i>Traditions</i> believe, and there is enough supporting evidence for it that they're not being foolish when they accept it as true. But by the same token, the Technocracy needs to have an alternative to the Purple Paradigm with its own supporting evidence so that <i>their</i> worldview <i>also</i> isn't obviously foolish for ignoring a blatant Truth about reality. This wasn't so much of a concern in the early days of the game when the Traditions were the game's protagonists and the Technocracy existed solely as a monolithic oppressor for them to fight against; but the more the game has evolved, the more it has tried to make the Technocrats viable alternatives for the game's protagonists. And as of M20, with the decoupling of Focus from faction and the possibility of playing Enlightened Scientists who are in no way associated with either the Union <i>or</i> the Traditions, it's even more important that what the Union calls Enlightened Science not be obviously flawed. And in that role, Scientists can't be, as I tend to phrase it, all liars or dupes: \u201cliars\u201d for those who understand that the Traditions are right but pretend that they aren't, and \u201cdupes\u201d for those who have bought into the lies. <br /> <br /> So how do you set up a world in which two seemingly opposed views about the fundamental nature of reality can <i>both</i> potentially be true? Very carefully; you have to thread the needle. And the first thing that you have to do is to remove the notion that either of their views <i>is</i> absolutely true. In order for there to be the possibility that the Technocrats might be <i>right</i>, there must also be the possibility that the Traditions might be <i>wrong</i>. And vice versa. So the ultimate Truth of the nature of reality can't be known; it must still be up for debate, as much as both the Traditions and the Technocracy might think otherwise. <br /> <br /> Then you need to construct a worldview for Enlightened Science that, while being opposed to the worldview of Awakened Magick, isn't brittle and overly simplistic and thus easily disproven. In particular, it shouldn't deny that what the Traditions do is possible; just that it's not what the Technocrats do, and that there are good reasons why not. To deny the evidence in front of your eyes would be insane. <br /> <br /> Which is where the innovation of dividing Quiet up into multiple types factors in: like it or not, there <i>are</i> Technocrats who hold a belief system that's incompatible with reality \u2014 the aforementioned liars and dupes from earlier editions. My take on them is first, that they're wearing metaphysical blinders \u2014 what MRev called Clarity and what M20 calls Denial \u2014 and second, that they're in the minority. A <i>loud</i> minority that gives the entire Union a bad reputation; but still a minority. <br /> <br /> This not only explains the earliest takes on the Technocracy's perspective, it also lets you use the Union in that way even in the modern, more enlightened interpretation: if you want a cabal of Traditionists to throw down against a construct of Unionists who unironically refer to them as Superstitionists and don't believe that Magick is real, just say that they've succumbed to Denial. Maybe even throw in a Negation Man or two into the mix just to make them a bit more dangerous. <br /> <br /> But again, that should be a minority view in the modern take on the Technocracy. The modern Technocrat should allow that magick is real, but it's not what Technocrats do. And if magick has benefits that Enlightened Science lacks, then the opposite should also be true. Fortunately, even by the rules as written, it is. Where Traditionalists can surpass their instruments, Technocrats can mass-produce Wonders. I like to supplement that with them also having an easier time instructing Extraordinary Citizens to use Adjustments (see my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/3491-acolyte-magic\">Acolyte Magic</a> hack), both because Extraordinary Citizens with a Technocratic mindset are more common than adepts with a Traditionist mindset and because the Union has superior teaching techniques; and there's even official support for something like <i>that</i>, in Sorcerer 20: there's a box that says that mages can use the rules for creating Talismans to create Paths; so the comparative ease with which Technocrats can create Devices translates to an easier process of creating new Paths of techno-sorcery. This gives a practical reason, not just an ideological one, for the Union to prefer Enlightened Science. It also serves as a challenge to the Traditions' ecumenical notions such as the \u201cWe Are All Gods In Disguise\u201d Paradigm, reinforcing the idea that they might be wrong. On the other hand, the fact that a Technocrat can become a Traditionist and vice versa challenges this notion that Enlightened Science and Awakened Magick are two different things. Both sides have ways of resolving the dilemmas posed to them; so the debate continues. <br /> <br /> So, what is this worldview that Enlightened Scientists hold? At it's heart, it's that the key to what they do isn't Willpower; it's Enlightenment. There <i>are</i> objective laws that reality obeys; but they're complex, and have many edge cases. Enlightened Science involves identifying those edge cases and using their instruments to exploit them. In that way, Tech Holds All Answers. To the extent that Willpower matters, it's only in the sense that Science requires self-discipline. <br /> <br /> The average Technocrat doesn't believe that what he himself does involves altering reality by belief and will; rather, the keys that the Technocrat possesses are enlightenment and discipline: knowledge of what <i>is</i> instead of belief in what one <i>wants to be</i>, and precise application of that knowledge rather than bending reality to your will. He'll even acknowledge that what a <i>mage</i> does involves imposing one's beliefs on reality by force of will \u2014 and that that's inherently dangerous and not the sort of thing that <i>he</i> would ever dabble in, thank you very much. <br /> <br /> (In that regard, I would be inclined to implement a house rule that removes the Willpower cap on Enlightenment, but mandates an Ability cap on Procedures and Adjustments: if you want to perform a four-dot Procedure, you must have four dots in a relevant Ability, probably chosen from the Abilities associated with your Practice. The limiting factor for Enlightened Science isn't willpower; it's talent, skill, and knowledge.)<br /> <br /> Also: on both sides of the debate, not every Focus needs to be able to explain what everyone <i>else</i> does in terms of their own beliefs or understanding; though that's a laudable goal if you can achieve it. They need only acknowledge that other ways also work, even if you personally find them unacceptable. A Verbena doesn't need to be able to explain what a Virtual Adept is doing in terms of her views about witchcraft; she need only accept that what the VA does <i>works</i>. Your Focus need only explain what <i>you</i> do; there's no obligation for it to explain what <i>others</i> do. <br /> <br /> And frankly, thinking that you <i>have</i> to explain everything in terms of your own Focus is a trap that <i>both</i> the Traditions and the Technocracy have fallen into, albeit in radically different and opposed ways. This is arguably where the <i>Disparates</i> have a valid point, as they don't even <i>attempt</i> some Grand Unified Theory of Magick (or Science, for that matter).<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's also the matter of Avatar vs. Genius, as well as Supernatural Merits and Flaws, and Backgrounds. It is entirely possible to conceptualize a mage's Avatar as something that's entirely distinct from the character, using Merits, Flaws, and Backgrounds: for instance, a mage with the Phylactery Flaw could have as his Avatar a wand: not merely a Unique Personal Instrument that lets him focus his Magick, but also quite literally the <i>source</i> of his Magick; or with the Manifest Avatar and the Familiar Background, you could make a Magickal Girl who was granted her powers by a cute talking animal. <br /> <br /> These are <i>not</i> things that are compatible with Enlightened Science. Genius is <i>never</i> independently manifested; it is, in fact, so subtle of a thing that it only ever manifests in ways that can't easily be distinguished from aspects of the Scientist's own psychology. The effects of the Circumspect Avatar Merit should be quite common among Enlightened Scientists, possibly so much so that anyone with Enlightenment should get them for free. <br /> <br /> More generally, this overall lack of most Supernatural Merits and Flaws in Enlightened Scientists can be pointed to as another bit of evidence for the Technocratic assertion that Science and Magick are separate things. Traditions would tend to counter that by saying that Genius is merely a restricted Avatar, with the Conditioning procedure suppressing supernatural manifestations where it's possible to do so. So again, the debate continues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-13-2022, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T12:54:59-07:00","id":1492821,"title":"","content":"This seems overly convoluted (yeah, I know, we're talking about Mage.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm biased against any attempt to seriously discuss things that starts with asserting that the concept of the Purple Paradigm is valuable. It's not actually what the Traditions believe. It's a fan-theory that mistakes rules-as-reality instead of rules-as-abstraction.<br /> <br /> That all said, I'm honestly surprised you completely skipped the simple answer: Earthly Foundations (or whatever term you want to use for them). The presence of these Foundations in the setting is everything you need for Enlightened Science to exist seriously, as there are constants in the Mage universe that no amount of will or subjective thinking can change. If there are immutable aspects of reality regardless of the impact of belief upon reality, then you have a solid basis for a scientific approach to a reality that seems to be at odds with science.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:10:14-07:00","id":1492830,"title":"","content":"I think it is first useful to define what exactly the Purple Paradigm is: it is the Hermetic paradigm. Not just in-game, but the actual real life base philosophy of modern Hermeticism. It has informed design because of this lens and is in-game the actual Paradigm for the Order of Hermes. It is at the same time useful as a means to explain the basics of the game, but not something any group within the game believes, <i>except</i>\u200b the OoH. Beyond that, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, it is a result of the all-too-common misunderstanding of game abstractions.<br /> <br /> Other than that, its most basic premise is perfectly valid in the game and for everyone, including the Union: Will can alter Reality. Accepting that, and that your own Paradigm runs with it, does not in any way means accepting that this is all there is to known about the universe and magic. Only the Order do put this idea as their main point and <i>believes</i> there's no limit. Everyone else can live with the idea that willpower is a real force, but this is only one aspect of reality.<br /> <br /> And I see no need to divorce what the Union does from what the Traditions do. The Union definitely isn't just applying discipline and precision in lieu of willpower over nature. Otherwise they would be just scientists, not Scientists! Instead, their particular proposition of why will shapes reality just needs to tell them that shaping it through pseudo-almost-science three-fold benefits: it's easier, safer and desirable.<br /> <br /> Desirable for what? To shape the Consensus. It doesn't really matters if the Consensus is all powerful or just another little piece of nature, they have a project to shape it and an invested interest in keeping it in their intended direction. You don't need any other reason to never do magic without tech than knowing that this is your part in the ongoing effort to keep reality stable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T14:18:06-07:00","id":1492831,"title":"","content":"While I didn't mention the Earthly Foundations by name, that's what I was referring to when I said that \u201cthere <i>are</i> objective laws that reality obeys\u201d. Building on the Earthly Foundations is at the heart of Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> I also don't agree with you about the Purple Paradigm never having been what the Traditions believe. In previous editions, at least, out was the glue that held the Traditions together. Even in M20 (specifically, Book of Secrets, in the entry for \u201cWe're All God(s) in Disguise\u201d), we get this:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">As a reflection of one of <b>Mage</b>'s primary themes, this paradigm is among the most \u201ctrue\u201d in meta terms. A character with this insight looks past the artificial divisions of <b>Mage</b>'s setting and views the fundamental unity expressed by the sentiment \u201cWe're <i>all</i> mages.\u201d As expressions of the shared gaming group and its players, mages with this perspective <i>are</i> seeing some of the truth of their situation. How true it is within the gaming world itself is for the Storyteller to decide, but this creed certainly rings true for mystics and philosophers throughout history who've chosen to ignore our mortal separations in favor of the living miracle of Creation itself.</div>For a game that goes out of its way to tell you that it's <i>your</i> game to do with as you will, that comes awfully close to flat out saying \u201cthis is true\u201d. <br /> <br /> Earlier editions were more explicit about it. <b>Guide to the Traditions</b> made a point to emphasize that the Traditions have learned over the centuries to work together, and that they say least pay lip service to the notion that it's ultimately all the same thing; and <i>every</i> edition prior to M20 described the discarding of foci as the mage gradually internalizing this truth and transcending her paradigm. <b>Masters of the Art</b> went so far as to suggest that not letting go of your paradigm was a good way to prevent you from achieving Ascension. Ironically, you can even do that in M20, where the concept has been flipped on its head and increased Arete now represents a deeper gut-level understanding and embrace of your Focus: for the Traditions, it means that something to the effect of \u201cWe're All God(s) in Disguise\u201d is part of their Paradigms, and so embracing their Focus more fully means embracing this creed more fully. <br /> <br /> Plus, there's mention in many of the <b>Mage</b> books that, for example, the Spheres are actual terms used by the Traditions as part of a sort of lingua franca; a way that makes from vastly different Traditions and who hold very different beliefs can communicate with each other well enough to collaborate on magickal workings. Again, before M20 there was mention that the Council of Nine featured nine Seats, each named after a different Sphere. This has gradually been downplayed over the years, to the point that it's not even mentioned in M20; but it's technically still there if you want to use it. <br /> <br /> I take the Purple Paradigm seriously because <b>Mage</b> takes it seriously. But at the end of the day, I reject it. It causes too many problems if accepted as ironclad fact. I <i>can</i>, however, buy that the <i>Traditions</i> accept it on some level \u2014 in part because it helps distinguish them from the Disparates. The Traditions favor a \u201cmelting pot\u201d style of cooperation; the Disparates, when they cooperate at all, prefer more of a \u201csalad bowl\u201d model, with each Craft jealously guarding its own identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T15:20:01-07:00","id":1492840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1492830#post1492830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is first useful to define what exactly the Purple Paradigm is: it is the Hermetic paradigm. Not just in-game, but the actual real life base philosophy of modern Hermeticism. It has informed design because of this lens and is in-game the actual Paradigm for the Order of Hermes. It is at the same time useful as a means to explain the basics of the game, but not something any group within the game believes, <i>except</i>\u200b the OoH. Beyond that, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, it is a result of the all-too-common misunderstanding of game abstractions.<br /> <br /> Other than that, its most basic premise is perfectly valid in the game and for everyone, including the Union: Will can alter Reality. Accepting that, and that your own Paradigm runs with it, does not in any way means accepting that this is all there is to known about the universe and magic. Only the Order do put this idea as their main point and <i>believes</i> there's no limit. Everyone else can live with the idea that willpower is a real force, but this is only one aspect of reality.<br /> <br /> And I see no need to divorce what the Union does from what the Traditions do. The Union definitely isn't just applying discipline and precision in lieu of willpower over nature. Otherwise they would be just scientists, not Scientists! Instead, their particular proposition of why will shapes reality just needs to tell them that shaping it through pseudo-almost-science three-fold benefits: it's easier, safer and desirable.<br /> <br /> Desirable for what? To shape the Consensus. It doesn't really matters if the Consensus is all powerful or just another little piece of nature, they have a project to shape it and an invested interest in keeping it in their intended direction. You don't need any other reason to never do magic without tech than knowing that this is your part in the ongoing effort to keep reality stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, you're stating the position of the Traditions and asserting that they're right. <br /> <br /> But while <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> has said that Technocrats know that they're shaping reality, it also says that they will deny to their dying breath that they're doing the same thing that mages do: the Disputed Data box on page 29 goes into great depth about how the Technocracy will never admit that what they do is the same as what the Superstitionists do. There, it's phrased in terms of denial of the truth; and the whole point of my original post here is to retain that conclusion (that Awakened Magick and Enlightened Science are two different things) as a valid possibility, ditching the implication that it's wrong. I'm also giving more detail about <i>how</i> they think what they do differs from what mages do: changing Arete to Enlightenment isn't just for flavor. <br /> <br /> Making Enlightened Science something that works off of talent, skill, and knowledge instead of willpower does that: Enlightened Scientists <i>are</i> capable of shaping reality; and the NWO in particular likes to shape hearts and minds. But they don't do it as Willworking; they don't bend reality to their will. Their means of altering reality are, at the core, less about motivation and more about technique. It's why they can never just push through on willpower alone (as mystics can when they Work Without Focus); but it's also why they can create Devices and Principia (and, by extension, techno-sorcery Paths) without having to expend personal Quintessence or a dot of Willpower in the process. All I'm doing with my <i>very trivial</i> house rule is taking that another step.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-11-2022, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T21:41:08-07:00","id":1492858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1492840#post1492840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, you're stating the position of the Traditions and asserting that they're right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> The difference is between saying &quot;We can impose our will upon reality because that's the Ultimate Truth of how reality works&quot; and saying &quot;We can impose our will upon <i>what we think</i> to be reality <i>to a certain extent</i>, because that's <i>an incidental consequence of some of reality's laws</i>&quot;. It is like the difference between saying that a balloon flies because hot air is less dense and saying it flies because it becomes saturated with negatively-weighted phlogiston. The similarity of the end result does not make them the same paradigm.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, that will shapes reality <b>is</b> right. Because that's how the game works regardless.of why. All the Mages live in a world where some people can demonstrably impose their will upon reality. They demonstrably can cause things to happen that wouldn't anyone else were to follow the exact same procedures. And this is equally true for all of them. However easier it is for Technocrats to create Paths and whatnot, it remains true that <b>they</b><b> are personally</b> a crucial piece to the process, something that flies in the face of any more technical definition of what they do, since <i>that</i> would mean normal people are simply incapable of following scientific procedures. Then <i>Enlightenment</i> would just mean that in the setting basic competence is a superpower.<br /> <br /> Reality works because it works. However scientists are needed to understand physics and come to the idea on how to build a laser, anyone can follow the instructions and build a laser with the appropriate tools. Because the phenomenon of the laser depends solely on the materials, built and powering of the device. What the Union does, just as what the Traditions do, demonstrably depends on some aspect of the person. It is easier to describe as will, it may even be something else. But it is unavoidably intrinsic to the person. <b>That</b> is the common thread the Order of Hermes calls will and codified into Arete and Spheres as a means of communication. And that's the aspect that no one needs to accept as the core principle of reality, as really working as the OoH says it does, or any of their other ideas about it to accept the simpler truth that it exists.<br /> <br /> You also put a lot of weight into the Traditions as a whole for metaphysical theory, ignoring that at the end of the day the Traditions are, and have always been, a political body. It needs a unifying manifesto because it needs common ground to state their collective purpose. They need the tools to enable coordination. They need a common language so they can both work together and share knowledge. They <b>don't </b>need to really believe in those ideas. As you said yourself, they only need to pay lip service to them.<br /> <br /> So the Purple Paradigm is three things within the game: it is a game design, something the authors maybe intended to be true to some degree but most importantly ensures all the <i>players</i> know and follow the same rules. It is a <b>demonstrable </b>fact of reality, but only in a very limited sense in that all characters know something intrinsic to their persons is key to any and all of those &quot;paradigm&quot; things to work. And it is an idea specific to a small group that was expanded as the political flag of a greater organization, regardless if its members really believe in it as magic theory or not.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that pointing to what happens at higher Arete levels means little to paradigm. As the books themselves explain, those are rules about how the character <i>transcends the basic assumptions</i> of their paradigm, however you interpret that to be as going deeper in it or beyond it. By definition this is not a representation of what the Traditions believe, it is a representation of what Mages do when they personally grow beyond such initial beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T23:52:23-07:00","id":1492866,"title":"","content":"\u2026and I lost a rather lengthy and in-depth response I was typing up. I don't feel like typing that all in again right now; so let's just go with a pair of points:<br /> <br /> 1. \u201cthey have an intrinsic quality that lets them shape reality\u201d doesn't mean that that intrinsic quality has anything to do with will. My contention is that Technocrats believe that it <i>isn't</i> will where Enlightened Science is concerned; it's something else. <i>And they're not necessarily wrong.</i> I've nominated \u201ctalent, skill, or knowledge\u201d instead of willpower as the thing that they rely on to shape reality. <br /> <br /> 2. The fact that there's a necessary intrinsic quality is <i>not</i> demonstrable. The capacity to create Paths, and the \u201cManagement and Human Resources\u201d optional rule (M20 p.595) or the \u201cPersonnel\u201d Instrument from the Syndicate Convention Book can be used to leverage the existing game mechanics to model the idea that Procedures <i>can</i> be taught to anyone who puts in the necessary work to learn them, and that anyone can can successfully perform a Procedure under the guidance of a competent teacher: <br /> <br /> \u201cThe Procedure can be taught to anyone who puts in the necessary work to learn it\u201d involves the teacher first putting in the necessary effort to prepare proper lesson plans (in game terms, he creates a techno-sorcery Path based on the Procedure), and then the pupil following those lesson plans until he gets the hang of it (buying that Path with XP). <br /> <br /> \u201cThe Procedure can be successfully performed by anyone under the guidance of a competent teacher\u201d is done by having the <i>teacher</i> technically be the one who's performing the Procedure as far as the game mechanics are concerned (i.e., you use the teacher's Enlightenment to roll for the success of the Procedure); but doing so indirectly, using the pupil as one of his Instruments by serving as a proxy for him. <br /> <br /> If you can't copy what the Scientist is doing and get the same results, it's probably not that he has some sort of superhuman power; it's probably that the Procedure you're attempting is very hard to get right, and you haven't gotten it right: you may <i>think</i> you did exactly what he did; but <i>did</i> you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T00:59:04-07:00","id":1492868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1492866#post1492866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and I lost a rather lengthy and in-depth response I was typing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel your loss, deeply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1492866#post1492866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. \u201cthey have an intrinsic quality that lets them shape reality\u201d doesn't mean that that intrinsic quality has anything to do with will. My contention is that Technocrats believe that it <i>isn't</i> will where Enlightened Science is concerned; it's something else. <i>And they're not necessarily wrong.</i> I've nominated \u201ctalent, skill, or knowledge\u201d instead of willpower as the thing that they rely on to shape reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I precisely meant that &quot;will&quot; may very well be accepted just as a placeholder. But let's make a quick analysis here.<br /> <br /> When you say &quot;talent, skill and knowledge&quot; you're describing the requirements for the actor to be effective at the action. But there's no direct link between those requirements and the end result in a naturalistic reality (science assumes a naturalistic reality). A shooter may have talent, skill and/or knowledge that makes them effective, but it isn't the talent, skill or knowledge that kills the target, it is a bullet propelled by an explosion at an angle and with a given momentum.<br /> <br /> Give me an intrinsic property of the person that can be theorized as causal to the phenomenon and couldn't be understood, if only at a shallow observation, as will?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1492866#post1492866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The fact that there's a necessary intrinsic quality is <i>not</i> demonstrable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you apply optional rules, it is. Either that, or the other problem I pointed: basic competence is a superpower.<br /> <br /> Technocrats make phaser guns out of garbage and high-tech leftovers that have no coherent design, and they frequently can't agree on how it works. They develop &quot;science&quot; that is unlike anything any other scientist can agree with, usually based on techno-babble they put together on the spot. And while they're able to use similarly fantastic methods to condition someone into replicating some of those stuff or to mass-produce their shenanigans, most people in the world simply can't replicate it even with the best tools, technical knowledge and dedication. Unless they go through the specific process to teach them that Procedure, which is an Enlightened Act in itself, the person is incapable of replicating <i>a procedure</i> and get the same effects.<br /> <br /> All the while it is known that the Enlightened have the same capacity as the Traditionalists for Magic if they put their minds to it, so much so that Conditioning enemies and people changing sides is a thing.<br /> <br /> I'm arguing that &quot;will unto reality&quot; doesn't have to mean the Union is fundamentally wrong, because the Earthly Foundation do exist, nature does have laws, normal science exists and works, there is enough evidence that the universe is naturalistic and the possibility of few select individuals affecting reality through &quot;will&quot; is just another piece. The piece that sets them apart from other people, but not necessarily a really important piece of how the universe works.<br /> <br /> But saying that they're fundamentally right in that it is just precise application of the laws of the universe and no such &quot;will on matter&quot; exists in their own practices does mean that what they're doing is true science and the masses are just too stupid to execute a Procedure without such an effort that the game literally demands new rules for teaching them technical skills.<br /> <br /> So I do agree with you that the take in the books that the Union is silly in dismissing Magic isn't the best one, a leftover still from the earlier take on them. But I also think your proposal is fully unnecessary to address it and it either fails to explain what Enlightenment is if it isn't the same thing as Arete, misrepresent the Traditions to think they all agree in a definition of will and magic they don't outside their political manifesto to make the Union seems like the only ones to reach another conclusion, or it defines Enlightenment as simply being competent enough to make real science, which I think makes the setting all the poorer, not richer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T10:55:48-07:00","id":1492898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick#post1492820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is the Purple Paradigm True?<br /> <br /> From the beginning of Mage, there has been the notion that the truth of the setting is that reality is fundamentally subjective, that Magick is enlightened will altering reality, and that Science is Magick. It's so prevalent that it's unofficially been given the name \u201cthe Purple Paradigm\u201d (after the color of the core book). I don't buy it; not as an absolute, incontrovertible truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the Purple Paradigm usually means. Purple Paradigm is generally a term for the oddness of game rules and abstractions being used as actual in universe paradigm. It was most often used to describe the hazy, wishcasting paradigm some players thought High Arete Mages defaulted to. &quot;Everything is subjective so anything is possible if you know the right Spheres&quot; and that kind of thing. It's been fading as an argument since M20 was more clear that Mages were internalizing foci rather than shedding them. <br /> <br /> It's not wrong to use the term here, per se - you are discussing the connection between the Traditions party line and the actual metaphysics of the game- but I wouldn't. The term Purple Paradigm has some baggage. <br /> <br /> As for your question, my answer depends on what you mean.<br /> <br /> If you mean, is the Traditions in-universe explanation of subjective reality true? Well, no, almost certainly not. The broad definition of it the books provide <i>might</i> be (that depends on the table), but only in the way &quot;Every Action has an Equal and Opposite Reaction&quot; is an adequate description of our world. The more intricate explanations the Traditions have in-universe are certainly inaccurate. The more honest Traditions Mages would even tell you that. They think they know the basic idea, but they simply don't know enough about how it works yet. <br /> <br /> The same is true for the Technocrats. They may be building on the more stable elements of reality but in-universe they have no way of knowing if those elements are more true. It's kind of like when we say the scientific method helps us see how the world works. It doesn't. It helps us predict how the world will act. We assume there is no difference but we can't be sure.<br /> <br /> I'm less certain the Traditions are right about Will, but that's almost explicitly stated to be an in universe kludge for helping them work together. Half the members of the Traditions wouldn't use the word Will to describe what they do. We can say, though, Mages and Technocrats are the same kind of thing and they have the same abilities. We know they can convert between each other without something as monumental as the Cauls or going Marauder. What differences they have are not of ability, but of approach. They may or may not 'cast spells' the same way, but if not then both ways are innate to the awakened condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:01:40-07:00","id":1492915,"title":"","content":"This is why I love the &quot;Enlightened Anthropic Principle&quot; (see Void Engineers Revised, p.53-54); it explains beautifully why the (Masses) Consensus affect Conventional Space, and why Technocrats in fact DO &lt;Willworking&gt; (a.k.a. &quot;Magick&quot;). I think it should be the main &quot;de-facto Paradigm&quot; of Highest-level Technocrats, because these guys &lt;know&gt; that what they do is metaphysically the same thing the Traditions do, only through different means; they know they are not simply &quot;discovering&quot; and &quot;harnessing&quot; reality, they know they are actually creating new &quot;nature laws&quot; when they work.<br /> <br /> PS: I understand that some people may want to make Enlightenment and Arete objectively different, but this will require House Rules and &quot;House Lore&quot;. I'm just talking about vanilla canon here; not about what could or should be, but about what it is now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 09-12-2022, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:29:32-07:00","id":1492921,"title":"","content":"I'm just reminded of <a href=\"https://i.redd.it/ebyxjjqohwt21.png\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> when talking about Enlightened Science in comparison to Magick.<br /> <br /> I think ultimiately it comes down to how Science is use in MtA and what it means to be a Mage. I think Sir Arthur Clarke's Three laws from Profiles of the Future are the best place to explain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Arthur Clarke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a distinguished but elderly scientist states that something is possible, he is almost certainly right. When he states that something is impossible, he is very probably wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Science has to end point. To quote Wikipedia &quot;Science is a systematic enterprise that builds and organizes knowledge in the form of testable explanations and predictions about the universe.&quot; In that aspect Enlightened Science would/should be &quot;a systematic enterprise that builds and organizes Hyper knowledge the form of testable explanations and predictions about the Meta-universe.&quot; So in relation to that definition Magick would be &quot;a chaotic enterprise that builds occultism in the form of untestable statements and declarations about the Meta-universe.&quot; Of course, as ultimate observers of the mechanics of WoD, we know that Magick is just the same Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> This of course isn't how Science is used in MtA. Science is used as a tool to make Magick against &quot;Consensus.&quot; No magical event could be truly explained by Science but it's good enough for the general population. So as the above picture, the only reason why 'Bone Magic' isn't vulgar is because of the Science. Of course under MtA, we know that it's both and that is what 'Purple Paradigm' means. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Arthur Clarke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way of discovering the limits of the possible is to venture a little way past them into the impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what does it mean to be an Enlightened Scientist? What does it mean to be a Master of the TU? If you are going to take the stance of 'One Truth' then what does it mean to do experiments to expand the knowledge? If a Technocrat takes the stance that anything outside of the preview of testable is impossible then what does it mean to progress understanding of universal laws? I don't think that MtA is equipped to answer these questions because I don't think it has a good foundation to build these questions off of. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sir Arthur Clarke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's bone magic. It's a privative version of steel. It's both. This is the most quoted of the laws and for good reason it's quick but, ultimately I believe that it's flawed without the other two laws. Understanding the impossible meta-physical laws of how the fundamental world of MtA works is what it means to follow 'purple paradigm', at least how I see it. It's understanding that both magic and science are tools used by people to preform a task and the only difference between the two is how your paradigm works and the arbitrary lines humans draw in the workings of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T04:59:50-07:00","id":1492970,"title":"","content":"Oh hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12895_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12895\" data-vbnamecard=\"12895\">MrNatas</a>! it has been a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T23:41:33-07:00","id":1493099,"title":"","content":"It's late and I wont have time to read it all, hopefully I'll do it tomorrow, and I'll also expand on my response, but just so I dont miss out in this discussion, I'll add very quickly my 2 cents<br /> <br /> Yes, I agree with DataWeaver, and I too would want to see Technocrats as Scientists pursuing the truth rather than a bunch of charlatans trying to hide it.<br /> <br /> My idea is: Quantum Superdeterminism.<br /> <br /> And yes, this is a real world theory, a theory for Quantum Mechanics that throw away all the nonsense about cats being both alive and dead at the same time, and puts the Quantum world back in the deterministic field. And there's also the Pilot Wave Theory that goes in that direction, which explain how quantum things can behave both as particles and waves simultaneously, in a determimistic way.<br /> <br /> What does that have to do with anything? Well, the universe not only is deterministic, but also absolutely interconnected.<br /> <br /> So, every single one of our thoughts produce electromagnetic energy, a field. We produce gravity.<br /> <br /> So, our mere existences influence the entire Universe.<br /> <br /> Now, we need only introduce a bit of the math on the Chaos Teory and the &quot;Butterfly Effect&quot;, and now we can explain every single &quot;psionic&quot; effects as a sort of manipulation of probabilities that build upon themselves in a butterfly effect.<br /> <br /> For example, lets say you think about fire. So, your thoughts about it generate an electromagnetic pulse, that pulse will slightly modify the air around, which, if caused in an exact way, can &quot;create&quot; a fireball.<br /> <br /> So, basically the Techie boys say that the Traditions just simply use &quot;psionic powers&quot;, albeit infected with &quot;superstitious nonsense&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T05:39:58-07:00","id":1493110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493099#post1493099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically the Techie boys say that the Traditions just simply use &quot;psionic powers&quot;, albeit infected with &quot;superstitious nonsense&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that fundamentally distinct from &quot;will alters reality&quot; instead of just an explanation of the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T07:42:00-07:00","id":1493113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493110#post1493110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that fundamentally distinct from &amp;quot;will alters reality&amp;quot; instead of just an explanation of the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. I was not trying to advocate for that - because it would not be possible to.<br /> <br /> Science is based on observation of the natural world, thus denying that the brain activity of a hermetic caused the air to combust would be to deny observation.<br /> <br /> Instead, my take is to say that &quot;magic(k) is just what hasnt been explained... yet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Therefore, instead of &quot;magic&quot; being the result of &quot;harmonic crystals&quot; lined up in geometric patterns to &quot;ressonate their vis&quot;, instead what you're doing is creating a quantum pattern that will induce a butterfly effect.<br /> <br /> It's not so much the &quot;will altering reality&quot;, and more of a &quot;reality hack&quot;.<br /> <br /> For example, let us say that you are sieging a medieval castle.<br /> <br /> You can throw several stones from trebuchets at it, and it will only cause minor damages.<br /> <br /> However, lets say that this castle have one tiny single point of weakness that, if hit in the perfect angle with the perfect force, it would crush the entire castle down, in a sort of domino effect.<br /> <br /> That's basically (in my alternative), the Techies would view &quot;magic&quot;, a series of domino effects upon reality, upon which small changes can be directed to generate large impacts.<br /> <br /> This would also coincidentally give more substance to the idea of being &quot;Enlightned&quot;. Those Scientists or... Urgh, &quot;mages&quot; (blergh, disgusting) would be people that became capable on acting instinctively on those subtle connections, subconciously managing to perceive those &quot;weak spots on reality&quot; and thus being able to use them in their favor.<br /> <br /> So, you are not exactly &quot;changing reality with your will&quot; - even if you are &quot;changing reality&quot; just with a meditation session, what you are actually doing isnt wishing reality to be, but rather attuning your brain electrons and molecules to the environment around you in order to ignite a chain reaction. It could also be achieved with crystals too, it doesnt even need to be your brain, it could be totally external, your brain is just a conduit, but the change is still fully materialistic, since it's NOT your &quot;will&quot;, but rather the configuration of your brain's particles that enact the change, but it can be done with crystals, herbs or machinery for example, in a process completely external. So, for example, let's say that lining up 5 quartz crystals in a pentagram makes a three of oak grow 2x faster. Why? Because you are lining up all the quantum probabilities in perfect harmony for that effect to take place.<br /> <br /> If that's true however, why cant just anyone do it? Or, why does it requires an Enlightned with the specific Sphere of Life?<br /> <br /> Because it aint just a matter of placing quartz crystals around a seed, they need to be placed in an exact position, which only an Enlightned person with the proper knowledge of Enlightned Life process will be able to <b>subconciously</b> do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T09:41:53-07:00","id":1493117,"title":"","content":"Interestingly many in the Traditions also make the claim that they are based on some kind of fundamental thing that is more real than the world. The Akashics claim to be descendents of the perfected wisdom of the inhabitants of Mount Meru, the Chorus seek the pieces of The One, and the Verbena claim inheritance of the Wyck. Notably all three are justifications for not writing those groups in accordance with the real world cultures they ostensibly represent. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T12:53:11-07:00","id":1493127,"title":"","content":"Question - how many of you have read any of Charles Stross' Laundry files books? The books take a highly scientific and technological approach to magic that would amaze some members of the Technocracy with its rigorousness, but the protagonists and practitioners in the book are well aware that what they are doing is 'magic'. The books are an excellent example of scientific magic.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Laundry_Files\" target=\"_blank\">The Laundry Files - Wikipedia</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T20:26:27-07:00","id":1493145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493113#post1493113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not. I was not trying to advocate for that - because it would not be possible to.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's the OP position.<br /> <br /> The discussion was not about how to explain the &quot;purple paradigm&quot; within the fiction, it was about Enlightenment being a fundamentally distinct phenomena from Arete, and tangentially if this is necessary to change the Union's presentation.<br /> <br /> Your proposal is perfectly valid as a sample Technocrat explanation for the phenomena of Awakening, but still completely within the game usual lore and rules, which is exactly what the OP proposes to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T22:49:06-07:00","id":1493200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493145#post1493145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's the OP position.<br /> <br /> The discussion was not about how to explain the &amp;quot;purple paradigm&amp;quot; within the fiction, it was about Enlightenment being a fundamentally distinct phenomena from Arete, and tangentially if this is necessary to change the Union's presentation.<br /> <br /> Your proposal is perfectly valid as a sample Technocrat explanation for the phenomena of Awakening, but still completely within the game usual lore and rules, which is exactly what the OP proposes to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Now Im confuse. Actually, I think I confused myself by confusing others with my answer. Because, after saying this which you pointed out, I believe I explained why this view wouldnt mean exactly willpower changing reality... I mean, the practical end result yes, would be the same, but not the actual meaning of &quot;will defines/change reality&quot;. In my proposal, it's not some ephemeral &quot;willpower&quot; disconnected from the physical world that alters reality, but instead it's a purely materialistic and mechanicist view of the world - upon which, even &quot;willpower&quot; becomes an absolutely mechanic phenomena - even a deterministic one.<br /> <br /> Blood hell, I think Im failing miserably to communicate, again.<br /> <br /> Please, let me know if this made an inch of more sense than before... Because it's late and Im beggining to confuse myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T01:38:34-07:00","id":1493208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493200#post1493200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, let me know if this made an inch of more sense than before... Because it's late and Im beggining to confuse myself</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the matter at hand isn't how the group explains &quot;magic&quot;, but making what each group does effectively distinct. Basically as if they were distinct splats with similar mechanics, instead of distinct approaches of the same splat.<br /> <br /> Not all Traditions mean &quot;willpower&quot; as a distinct phenomena from material reality, and even those that do aren't necessarily meaning it as outside natural reality, that is, they may very well believe will is some natural property within the world, maybe better described by another term, that causes changes through also natural processes. The ones that <b>do</b> believe reality is changed by will in a literal sense are some of the more traditional Hermetics, specifically. Otherwise, the definition it is more relevant as a political stance to unite the Council than an actual theory of magic.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, your idea basically presents a theory behind the phenomena, but still accepts the phenomena as being the same for Union and Traditions, an Awakened/Enlightened is what it is, whichever group they belong to. But the OP proposes making them distinct for real with the Union recognizing that &quot;will alters reality&quot; exists at least as observable phenomena, but effectively refuse to do the same and instead apply another mechanic entirely.<br /> <br /> So it is the opposite to what you're doing: in the books the Union says it does something completely different from what the RTs do, and since it isn't true in the game, they're delusional. You proposes that this isn't the case because they don't need to say such a thing (they have better things to say for their point). But the OP proposes this isn't the case because it is not actually a delusion, but the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T04:41:56-07:00","id":1493318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493208#post1493208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is the opposite to what you're doing: in the books the Union says it does something completely different from what the RTs do, and since it isn't true in the game, they're delusional. You proposes that this isn't the case because they don't need to say such a thing (they have better things to say for their point). But the OP proposes this isn't the case because it is not actually a delusion, but the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>To further the point, Mages have a lot of different reasons for how subjective reality works. Coming up with one for the Technocracy isn't the problem. The bigger question is why, knowing that, they would restrict themselves to a narrow range of doing things? Why would they be so certain that they are doing things the right way that they can't even drop instruments? Why would they spend so much time and energy working on the Consensus? It seems like they are trying to have it both ways: they are both scientists and technology is a paradigm they invented and are trying to convince the world of. <br /> <br /> Of course that only seems ridiculous if we assume reality is simply understood. <br /> <br /> A lot of people assume that Mage reality is obviously and simply subjective, so the Traditions are right and the Technocracy is engaged in ludicrous self deception. Others assume Mage reality is mostly based on modern physics and the consensus just creates the possibility of magic, so the Technocracy is right and the Traditions are in a futile and pointless struggle. Neither of these makes sense and neither fits with Mage as depicted. Indeed if the former were true, the Traditions would likely be a hodgepodge of magical ideas rather than the continuation of mostly faded cultural practices, and if the latter were true the Technocracy wouldn't be using the magic system at all.<br /> <br /> Instead what we see is a world that clearly has a consensus that affects reality itself, but we also see that most Mages (not just the Technocracy) do think that certain things are more true (or at least better). The implication is, the world is complicated and not fully understood and both the Traditions and the Technocracy are in some way right, no matter how much they seem to contradict each other. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T17:36:27-07:00","id":1493369,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not that thrilled at the idea of making Arete and and Enlightenment distinct. Yes, you can say right now that the Traditions are right and the Technocracy are wrong, but the solution of making what the Technocracy do distinct from 'Sphere Magic' seems to be....making the Technocracy right and the Traditions delusional for thinking that the Technocracy are doing the same things they are, which seems like a bit of a strange fix to the 'problem', at least to me. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T21:13:05-07:00","id":1493378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493208#post1493208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, the matter at hand isn't how the group explains &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot;, but making what each group does effectively distinct. Basically as if they were distinct splats with similar mechanics, instead of distinct approaches of the same splat.<br /> <br /> Not all Traditions mean &amp;quot;willpower&amp;quot; as a distinct phenomena from material reality, and even those that do aren't necessarily meaning it as outside natural reality, that is, they may very well believe will is some natural property within the world, maybe better described by another term, that causes changes through also natural processes. The ones that <b>do</b> believe reality is changed by will in a literal sense are some of the more traditional Hermetics, specifically. Otherwise, the definition it is more relevant as a political stance to unite the Council than an actual theory of magic.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, your idea basically presents a theory behind the phenomena, but still accepts the phenomena as being the same for Union and Traditions, an Awakened/Enlightened is what it is, whichever group they belong to. But the OP proposes making them distinct for real with the Union recognizing that &amp;quot;will alters reality&amp;quot; exists at least as observable phenomena, but effectively refuse to do the same and instead apply another mechanic entirely.<br /> <br /> So it is the opposite to what you're doing: in the books the Union says it does something completely different from what the RTs do, and since it isn't true in the game, they're delusional. You proposes that this isn't the case because they don't need to say such a thing (they have better things to say for their point). But the OP proposes this isn't the case because it is not actually a delusion, but the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now Im confuse. My idea was that Techies are &quot;scientists&quot; (\ud83d\ude09), therefore they should come up with theories that are at least based on observation; it gets a little bit difficult to deny &quot;magic&quot; as pure superstitious gibberish when that damn hermetic keeps throwing fireballs from thin air by agitating his arms like a fool. That gets a little hard to deny.<br /> <br /> So, our proudly &quot;superior&quot; techie boys need some kind of explanation as to how this could be. And some explanation that involves &quot;science&quot; and not all that &quot;spirit-magic-miracle&quot; &quot;nonsense&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's what I was trying to do... Otherwise, the techie boys are a bunch of liars who know that they are lying - which is completely fine too as a different premisse for a different type of conspiracy game, but I always thought that the idea was to make the techies believe their own bullshit.<br /> <br /> Anyway... I guess I missed the point. Im not understanding a damn thing. What is it exactly the the OP wanted? Because Im completely lost and confuse here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T02:06:29-07:00","id":1493392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493378#post1493378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway... I guess I missed the point. Im not understanding a damn thing. What is it exactly the the OP wanted? Because Im completely lost and confuse here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP wants to make Traditions and Technocracy work on distinct rules.<br /> <br /> Mildly distinct from pure mechanics standpoint, but irreconcilably distinct in the lore.<br /> <br /> Basically turn then into two distinct splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T12:53:20-07:00","id":1493422,"title":"","content":"As an idea for the &quot;House Lore&quot;:<br /> <br /> Two things being distinct doesn't mean they don't have the same root. Maybe what they do it's the same thing on some level, but not on another level.<br /> <br /> *The Avatar (whatever it may be) it's clearly important for both, Spirit 5 will de-power a Technocrat as good as anyone else's. Will it's important for both, you can't raise the bar that limits your Spheres w/o it, but it's more important for Traditionalists that can also use it as substitute for an Instrument.<br /> <br /> *One of the key differences between Mages magic(k) and Sorcerers magic, it's that the first *impose* their Will on reality to &quot;create&quot; magic (which does, still, employ and obey certain rules - those of uppercase Reality), and the latter employ existing undercurrents of magic (not Reality - per se - but also magics that are part of reality, like that which Mages can create).<br /> <br /> *Ironically, the faction that believes in &quot;science&quot; has been the one that <i>was able to impose their Will uppon reality more effectively</i>, and <i>actually changed what's real and what's not</i>. Not only by making stuff like planes real (allegedly against at least one Foundation) ... but also by making &quot;un-real&quot; a lot of *stuff that was real*, like dragons.<br /> But maybe that's why they would eschew Willworking...?<br /> <br /> *Philosophical scientist Francis Bacon said scientists needed to &quot;put lead to the wings of reason&quot;, to be like Dedalus and not like Icaro: Bacon proposed to submit research to a scientific community, to judge it, rather than to trust in the individual genius. This could be slower, but would make more solid conclusions that would make the building blocks of better science (Bacon was an alchemist, and this was a criticism against the way alchemists opperated: Bacon disliked how alchemists investigated alone, and then encrypted their discoveries)<br /> <br /> SO, maybe Technocrats do *limit* themselves, but not out of ignorance, rather because they would like to tune their Avatars into working with whatever powers are already there (the Foundations, but also what's already set as part of the world trough magick) to conjure more ... let's say ... &quot;rigurous changes&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe this <i>discipline </i>changed their relationship to magick in a way their works require a <i>substratum </i>of sorts (The Instrument) beyond the normal needs of Technomancy, but also are less dependant on their own Will (their ease with Wonders).<br /> <br /> So, what they do it's the same, but not the same. It's <i>at it's core </i>the same, but the Foucs of the Will it's irreconciliable and conditions the Avatar to work a certain way that it's most certainly different. And, in that sense, they could say that what they do isn't the same (You <i>force </i>your Will uppon reality, I use my Will to <i>manipulate </i>reality, we're not the same :P)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-20-2022, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-21T18:16:20-07:00","id":1493496,"title":"","content":"That's all well and good until you get to the part where other than the Hermetic Order, some of the Traditions are very much trying to 'work with what's there already', so it gets messy. Is Tradition/Order X working on Rules A or Rules B?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T05:48:31-07:00","id":1493526,"title":"","content":"Aye, that's a very good point.<br /> <br /> Like: it's the &quot;Word of God&quot; a Foundation equal or above those that we could call &quot;scientific facts&quot;?, Choristers that base their workings on <i>faith </i>should be able to produce Wonders like Technocrats?, not being able would imply the tenets of their faith wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T17:56:37-07:00","id":1493791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493392#post1493392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP wants to make Traditions and Technocracy work on distinct rules.<br /> <br /> Mildly distinct from pure mechanics standpoint, but irreconcilably distinct in the lore.<br /> <br /> Basically turn then into two distinct splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in... Turning Arete and Enlightenment into distinct features?<br /> <br /> Perhaps even with... One nullifying the other? (aka if you &quot;awaken&quot; your Arete, you cannot &quot;develop&quot; your Enlightment and vice-versa?)<br /> <br /> Hmm... That's actually... Not a bad idea, really.<br /> <br /> The downside is that it would no longer be possible to have &quot;conversions&quot;, like brainwashed trads turned techies... Which also aint so bad overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T23:25:24-07:00","id":1493957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493791#post1493791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As in... Turning Arete and Enlightenment into distinct features?<br /> <br /> Perhaps even with... One nullifying the other? (aka if you &quot;awaken&quot; your Arete, you cannot &quot;develop&quot; your Enlightment and vice-versa?)<br /> <br /> Hmm... That's actually... Not a bad idea, really.<br /> <br /> The downside is that it would no longer be possible to have &quot;conversions&quot;, like brainwashed trads turned techies... Which also aint so bad overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> It isn't a bad idea <i>per se</i>, it just doesn't address the problem that was pointed out. It isn't either helpful or needed. But can it be done and result in an interesting game? Sure, it can.<br /> <br /> My problem with it would be how to define science in a way that doesn't make actual scientists be the dumb fools in the setting, so it becomes Competence Is A Super Power. But that could be addressed with something similar to <i>Genius: the Transgression</i>. So, so much not a bad idea that there is a quite popular fan game built around it, already.<br /> <br /> But it isn't Mage's assumption and Mage doesn't need it to work, it would just be a different game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T05:08:37-07:00","id":1493969,"title":"","content":"Science is done in the dark in our world too. There are various assumptions in the method itself that we don't know are true and we press on with it anyways. If you look at the history of scientific theories, it is a hash of odd ideas, strange exceptions, and special pleading, and that's without looking at all the times scientists have unintentionally (or even intentionally) disregarded an element of the method and carried on as if nothing was amiss.<br /> <br /> The method was developed to deal with a world that we didn't (and honestly still don't) know would play along. It's going to have some utility even in a subjective reality. Even knowing that expectations and biases will affect the results doesn't make it completely invalid as that's something scientists already have to deal with (admittedly for psychological rather than metaphysical reasons) As long as there is at least some consistency and at least the appearance of underlying rules the scientific method or something like it will have a use.<br /> <br /> The only scenario that the Technocracy would be completely stupid (or evil) is if they knew for a fact that there was no underlying structure to reality and that complete nonsense would work as well as reasoned belief and yet they keep applying the method anyways. Even most marauders don't act like they believe that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there is a hidden bias that's messing us up on this argument. Traditions members have just as much internal consistency in their paradigms as the Technocracy has in theirs and if we knew what they really believed we'd probably think it was just as incompatible with subjective reality as the scientific method. We don't, though, so it looks like the Techies are the only ones hit by that issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T06:30:07-07:00","id":1493974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493969#post1493969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science is done in the dark in our world too. There are various assumptions in the method itself that we don't know are true and we press on with it anyways. If you look at the history of scientific theories, it is a hash of odd ideas, strange exceptions, and special pleading, and that's without looking at all the times scientists have unintentionally (or even intentionally) disregarded an element of the method and carried on as if nothing was amiss.<br /> <br /> The method was developed to deal with a world that we didn't (and honestly still don't) know would play along. It's going to have some utility even in a subjective reality. Even knowing that expectations and biases will affect the results doesn't make it completely invalid as that's something scientists already have to deal with (admittedly for psychological rather than metaphysical reasons) As long as there is at least some consistency and at least the appearance of underlying rules the scientific method or something like it will have a use.<br /> <br /> The only scenario that the Technocracy would be completely stupid (or evil) is if they knew for a fact that there was no underlying structure to reality and that complete nonsense would work as well as reasoned belief and yet they keep applying the method anyways. Even most marauders don't act like they believe that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there is a hidden bias that's messing us up on this argument. Traditions members have just as much internal consistency in their paradigms as the Technocracy has in theirs and if we knew what they really believed we'd probably think it was just as incompatible with subjective reality as the scientific method. We don't, though, so it looks like the Techies are the only ones hit by that issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect this is true. If I were to bet, I'd say that the Choristers view would either be that of an intelligible world devised by the One, or Berkeley's immaterialism that we are all only spritual beings and the &quot;material&quot; world is just a theater of the One's mind; that's not a subjective reality at all however, since it is all predicated on a single POV of the divine. I'd say that the Eutanathoi might actually have a similar opnion, at least if they hold some hinduistic views (as opposed to having nothing at all with it), in which the Universe is all part of Vishnu's will (or Vishnu's Dream) - also, hinduism is an interesting religion, in which in the end is sort of monotheistic while having literally millions of Gods, since each God is a manifestation, an Avatar, of a God above; even the higher triat, Vishnu, Bhrama and Shiva are the 3 aspects of the same forces of creation. Buddhism may actually be different here, since the entire premisse of buddhism is that we are all trapped in &quot;Maya&quot;, the dream, the illusion, and that this illusion is a consequence of our desires, and we must reach Nirvana and transcende it (by the way, the entire &quot;Ascension&quot; thing seems to be heavily inspired by budhism); this however doesnt translates to MtA letter by letter, but the Akashics are... Somewhat influenced by buddhism - actually, they are a sort of very superficial take inspired by Shaolin monks... Actually, not even that, but rather by Kung Fu MOVIES depictions of Shaolin Monks... But still, we could say that buddhism is there, and with it, perhaps or probably, this subjective perception of reality.<br /> <br /> As for the others it gets a bit harder. Well, actually I doubt that the Virtual Adepts believe that reality is subjective, in fact they may view it as even more &quot;solid&quot; (albeit not material) than the Techies themselves, since it's all information to them; for the Etherites thou... Well, for the Etherites this is probably a raging internal debate - just like we have quantum physicists that believe in the random nonsense that generates cats that are both dead and alive simultaneously, and others that believe in quantum Superdeterminism or the Pilot Wave Theory that erases completely all the nonsense of quantum physics (but the &quot;orthodoxes&quot; dont like it because this means that there is no &quot;free will&quot; - anyway, long story).<br /> <br /> Hermetics on the other way I'd say that lean more towards subjectivity of reality, at least if we base the game ones in the real world ones. The Dreamspeakers... Are complicated. I have some contact with Umbanda, which is a brazilian religion with african origin, that would probably be clumped up togheter with the Dreamspeakers. My wife is a practitioner and firm believer - yes, it's a funny combination, since she believes there are spirits everywhere watching her every move, while I am a staunch atheist, skeptical materialist. It's like a Techie boy marriaged to a Shaman. Anyway... I've even participated in several cerimonies with her, and I say, it is not a subjective worldview either. It's a polytheistic religion, with a very defined &quot;cosmological order&quot;. Now, I cant speak obviously for all native religions of south and north Americas, nor for Asian or African aboriginal animistic religions, but I would say that certanly in the game there wouldnt be a unified tenet around a subjective reality; the opposite however may hold true.<br /> <br /> As for the others, they arent my cup of tea, Verbena and Cult of Ecstasy, so I never learned them all too well, nor ever cared to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T14:09:05-07:00","id":1494345,"title":"","content":"<i>Disclaimer: Long rant, and English is not my first language.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can we be a bit more meta on the analysis? <br /> <br /> <br /> I am going to digress and complain a bit, but truly this is all because ignorant (although creative) writers started writing about things that they had no idea how work in real life. <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the inconsistencies of the setting Magick vs Science is due to simply ignorant writers... That equal science with a &quot;lack of soul&quot; or &quot;no poetry&quot;... It was a bit cartoonish, and that is where most of the problems originated. <b>Consensus is an internally inconsistent idea, most of the setting is internally inconsistent, so we are discussing about things that not even current writers can fix, without unmaking the setting itself.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> True real world science is not machines or devices, it is a process, it is analyzing how the world works without preconceptions, what it is not what I want it to be. <b>A real world scientist would have already hypothesized that belief is what powers Traditions and would have found that this hypothesis fits all different paradigms</b>, and explains Marauders, Traditionalist, and Technocracy beliefs.<br /> <br /> <br /> From there,<b> the next question from a real world scientist would be WHY belief modifies the universe, not which beliefs should be held.</b> The WHY would give you true power over magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea that Technocracy is winning because the masses believe in science, is... Dumb. Just plain dumb. Most of mankind is superstitious, religious in great deal, and/or completely ignorant how basic appliances work (let's not even talk about concepts like thermodynamics or special relativity). \u200bThe world should be more like a Cultivation novel, with plenty of magical beast, feudal lords, creatures... if the Consensus works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just to put some examples from other settings where bad writing makes the universe inconsistent, comic writers have Iron Man, a renowned industrialist, invent a portable communication device, lightweight materials, AND a portable high powered energy source... And the world is still the same! With just the technology necessary for the Iron Man suit (let's not even touch Reed Richards' tech, or Justice League tech in DC) any business consultant worth their salt would have changed the way computers, trains, cars, medical devices and life in general works.<br /> <br /> <br /> My comic example is to show how people trying to be &quot;creative&quot; but really not exploring the consequences of their hypothetical magic / technology, nor having any idea how a business work, or in the case of Mage the Ascension, not having any single clue how science works, at all, or not exploring the consequences of their ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>So all our threads and questions are going to be inconsistent because, to my great sorrow, the Mage the Ascension setting is poorly thought, badly designed, extremely inconsistent, and we are working upon almost 30 years of bad writing over a dumb start. We never are going to have good answers because the <i>setting</i> is just not good. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-04-2022, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T16:42:34-07:00","id":1494361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493422#post1493422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an idea for the &quot;House Lore&quot;:<br /> <br /> Two things being distinct doesn't mean they don't have the same root. Maybe what they do it's the same thing on some level, but not on another level.<br /> <br /> *The Avatar (whatever it may be) it's clearly important for both, Spirit 5 will de-power a Technocrat as good as anyone else's. Will it's important for both, you can't raise the bar that limits your Spheres w/o it, but it's more important for Traditionalists that can also use it as substitute for an Instrument.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reliance of Enlightenment on Willpower, BTW, was one of this things I was suggesting be changed via house ruling. In practice, it's not even a restriction for most mages, as they start out with Willpower 5 and so aren't going to run into the cap on the bar that limits their Spheres until they start eying the <i>Arch</i>spheres \u2014 something that's almost never going to come into play in most games, given just how much Mastery is capable of. <br /> <br /> The only other thing the Willpower cap limits is the size of your dice pool when working an Effect; and I'll grant that that's a more significant limitation. But even there, it only kicks in above Arete 5 \u2014 again, because there's no such thing as a mage with Willpower <i>below</i> 5. <br /> <br /> Except, of course, when there is: crafting a Talisman costs a dot of Willpower; so if a Willpower 5 mage makes a Talisman, he loses access to any Mastery-level Effects he used to have, until such time as he recovers that fifth dot of Willpower. The result of this is to make Talisman creation rare; because there's an indirect XP tax on each Talisman. <br /> <br /> But Enlightened Scientists don't have that problem; because they <i>don't</i> have to lose a dot of Willpower whenever they make a Device. So the Willpower cap is less problematic for them <i>here</i>, too. Removing the Willpower cap from Enlightenment entirely strike me as removing a limitation that doesn't really limit them. If anything, the imposition of Ability-based caps on all of their Enlightened workings strikes me as a more serious restriction. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493422#post1493422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*One of the key differences between Mages magic(k) and Sorcerers magic, it's that the first *impose* their Will on reality to &quot;create&quot; magic (which does, still, employ and obey certain rules - those of uppercase Reality), and the latter employ existing undercurrents of magic (not Reality - per se - but also magics that are part of reality, like that which Mages can create).</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I disagree with here is the insistence that the former involves imposing will. It certainly <i>does</i> involve <i>shaping</i> reality; but my contention is that, for Enlightened Scientists, it's not \u201cimposing Will\u201d. <br /> <br /> But since you've mentioned Sorcery, let me reiterate another point that I've made: <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> includes an option whereby the Talisman creation rules can be used to create <i>Paths</i>. And it mentions that the Technocracy has been particularly successful in employing this method to empower its Extraordinary Citizens. This difference between Talismans and Devices is part of why: an Awakened Mage who wants to forge a Path has to put a dot of Willpower into it; an Enlightened Scientist doing the same <i>doesn't</i>. By all rights, there should be techno-sorcery Paths galore coming out of the Technocracy's academic Laboratories. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493422#post1493422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Ironically, the faction that believes in &quot;science&quot; has been the one that <i>was able to impose their Will uppon reality more effectively</i>, and <i>actually changed what's real and what's not</i>. Not only by making stuff like planes real (allegedly against at least one Foundation) ... but also by making &quot;un-real&quot; a lot of *stuff that was real*, like dragons.<br /> But maybe that's why they would eschew Willworking...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, strike out the \u201cimpose their Will upon reality\u201d bit, and I agree with this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493422#post1493422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Philosophical scientist Francis Bacon said scientists needed to &quot;put lead to the wings of reason&quot;, to be like Dedalus and not like Icaro: Bacon proposed to submit research to a scientific community, to judge it, rather than to trust in the individual genius. This could be slower, but would make more solid conclusions that would make the building blocks of better science (Bacon was an alchemist, and this was a criticism against the way alchemists opperated: Bacon disliked how alchemists investigated alone, and then encrypted their discoveries)<br /> <br /> SO, maybe Technocrats do *limit* themselves, but not out of ignorance, rather because they would like to tune their Avatars into working with whatever powers are already there (the Foundations, but also what's already set as part of the world trough magick) to conjure more ... let's say ... &quot;rigurous changes&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe this <i>discipline </i>changed their relationship to magick in a way their works require a <i>substratum </i>of sorts (The Instrument) beyond the normal needs of Technomancy, but also are less dependant on their own Will (their ease with Wonders).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea that Enlightened Scientists have changed Avatars into Geniuses, with the difference being that Avatars are tied into Willpower while Geniuses\u2026 aren't. It's not entirely unlike the idea of how the Nephandi can <i>invert</i> an Avatar. And it brings another step of how Technocrats can view themselves as doing something fundamentally different from Mages, despite the ability to convert mages into Enlightened Scientists and vice versa: it's that the conversion process is more fundamental than \u201cjust\u201d changing your Focus. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493422#post1493422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what they do it's the same, but not the same. It's <i>at it's core </i>the same, but the Focus of the Will it's irreconciliable and conditions the Avatar to work a certain way that it's most certainly different. And, in that sense, they could say that what they do isn't the same (You <i>force </i>your Will uppon reality, I use my Will to <i>manipulate </i>reality, we're not the same :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the Traditional way of describing it, yes. The Enlightened Science view, on the other hand, scratches out the \u201cuse my Will to\u201d from that last part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-05-2022, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T00:13:14-07:00","id":1494395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1493791#post1493791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in... Turning Arete and Enlightenment into distinct features?<br /> <br /> Perhaps even with... One nullifying the other? (aka if you &quot;awaken&quot; your Arete, you cannot &quot;develop&quot; your Enlightment and vice-versa?)<br /> <br /> Hmm... That's actually... Not a bad idea, really.<br /> <br /> The downside is that it would no longer be possible to have &quot;conversions&quot;, like brainwashed trads turned techies... Which also aint so bad overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually <i>not</i> what I'm suggesting. At least not the \u201cyou can't convert one to the other\u201d part. What I <i>am</i> suggesting is to extend the <i>Blind Men and the Elephant</i> schtick to question whether or not the elephant is the only thing there: what if there's both an elephant and a rhino, for instance? How hard would it be, working strictly from the accounts of the blind men, to discount the latter possibility? With that said:<br /> <br /> Yes, I <i>am</i> suggesting the possibility that Arete and Enlightenment are two different, albeit incredibly similar, things: that Arete is about imposing your Will on reality (in a very literal way, where the basic premise involves Will directed by belief and shaped by practice and instruments), while Enlightenment <i>isn't</i>. From the Traditional standpoint, this might be explained as Enlightenment being Arete with self-discipline being imposed, a <i>refusal</i> to impose one's Will on reality, and instead to better understand the deeper mysteries of how the shaping of Reality works. The Enlightened Scientist, by contrast, would say that there's no refusal, per se; just an acknowledgement that there are ways to shape reality that don't involve applied Will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T00:38:54-07:00","id":1494397,"title":"","content":"I really struggle to see the benefit of this, as it boils down to trying to 'fix' the fact that the rules and lore as written imply that everything is a product of Will and the Technocrats are delusional...by making the Traditions delusional and the Technocrats right? It just swings the ball back the other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T03:21:28-07:00","id":1494401,"title":"","content":"You'd think so, right? But no. Traditionists can argue, with some merit, that despite the differences between an Avatar and a Genius (whatever they are), the fact that you can switch from one to the other means that they're essentially the same thing. <br /> <br /> Both sides have arguments going for them; and which is right (assuming either of them is) is ultimately something to be determined by the Storyteller (assuming the Storyteller wants to bother).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T06:35:43-07:00","id":1494414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494401#post1494401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd think so, right? But no. Traditionists can argue, with some merit, that despite the differences between an Avatar and a Genius (whatever they are), the fact that you can switch from one to the other means that they're essentially the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>A problem with &quot;Traditionalists can argue&quot; this: Technocrats are the ones that exercise that fact in the most forcefull and systematic way...unless they think room 101 *kills/supresses* the Avatar and *creates* a Genius (or awakens it, and somehow doesn't work if the target isn't &quot;Avatar user&quot; first?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T07:07:37-07:00","id":1494416,"title":"","content":"Transforms an Avatar into a Genius, from the Technocrat perspective. The Traditions most familiar with the process would view it as a <i>really mild</i> modification of the Avatar rather than as a transformation into something else. They might even view it as \u201cdamaging the Avatar\u201d, as the result <i>does</i> remove the ability to Work Without Focus; and the Traditions would likely zero in on that as the most important effect of Conditioning. They're likely to overlook the fact that that change also <i>enables</i> the Scientist to build Devices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-05-2022, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T07:07:47-07:00","id":1494417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494361#post1494361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This reliance of Enlightenment on Willpower, BTW, was one of this things I was suggesting be changed via house ruling. In practice, it's not even a restriction for most mages, as they start out with Willpower 5 and so aren't going to run into the cap on the bar that limits their Spheres until they start eying the <i>Arch</i>spheres \u2014 something that's almost never going to come into play in most games, given just how much Mastery is capable of.<br /> <br /> The only other thing the Willpower cap limits is the size of your dice pool when working an Effect; and I'll grant that that's a more significant limitation. But even there, it only kicks in above Arete 5 \u2014 again, because there's no such thing as a mage with Willpower <i>below</i> 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Other than Archspheres, Initiates of the Art had mages start with Willpower 3, but it's true that for 99% of Mage games you ain't seeing the limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except, of course, when there is: crafting a Talisman costs a dot of Willpower; so if a Willpower 5 mage makes a Talisman, he loses access to any Mastery-level Effects he used to have, until such time as he recovers that fifth dot of Willpower. The result of this is to make Talisman creation rare; because there's an indirect XP tax on each Talisman.<br /> <br /> But Enlightened Scientists don't have that problem; because they <i>don't</i> have to lose a dot of Willpower whenever they make a Device. So the Willpower cap is less problematic for them <i>here</i>, too. Removing the Willpower cap from Enlightenment entirely strike me as removing a limitation that doesn't really limit them. If anything, the imposition of Ability-based caps on all of their Enlightened workings strikes me as a more serious restriction. </div> </div> </div>Unless something changed since BoS, I have to disagree here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.161, BoS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocratic Union facilities produce Devices and Principiae without the Willpower or personal Quintessence requirements. <b>Individual </b>technomancers and <b>Technocrats</b>, however, <b>must invest Willpower and personal Quintessence into their Devices</b>. Only specialized personnel are allowed access to these facilities; abuse of such access is deeply unmutual.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, it isn't their Enligthenment, but the &quot;facilities&quot; of the Union, what allows Technocrats this advantage. Technocrats doing this on their own still have to use their Willpower...<br /> <br /> This is a very real limitation, because it means you need to be part of a very specific Faction, and you can be denied access if you start going rogeish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-05-2022, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T07:25:11-07:00","id":1494419,"title":"","content":"Those Facilities don't just pop up out of nowhere; they have to be built. My premise here is that setting up a \u201cmass production line\u201d (which is what you use to make Devices without the usual Willpower or Personal Quintessence requirements) is something that only the Enlightened can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T07:45:49-07:00","id":1494421,"title":"","content":"It's still something important to note. A rogue Technocrat may be &quot;on his own&quot;, but still could have the Resources to build a small factory, the magick to make wonders, and the Instrumental inclination. Still the book seems to imply that having money and a dream isn't enough for the Enligthened.<br /> <br /> We don't know, but it would be useful to know, if all that it takes is this instrument and Enligthenment (then any individual Technocrat so inclined can make a &quot;Technocratic Union Facility&quot;), if it's in and of itself a powerful Wonder, or secret work of magick like Primium (then you also need to be powerful?, Archmastery even?), or what...<br /> Depending on what's going on, <i>this is or isn't a problem for individual Technocrats</i>. Whereas a rogue faction (like, say, Navalon) could be up the task...or maybe not even (the book specifies TU facilities...).<br /> <br /> Morover, if Technocrats <i>aren't</i> using Will to alter reality...<i>then they shouldn't be able to invest their Will on Devices when they're on their own.</i> No?. It's either X or Y, not X when you don't care about it, but Y under durance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-05-2022, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T16:40:18-07:00","id":1494438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't know, but it would be useful to know, if all that it takes is this instrument and Enligthenment (then any individual Technocrat so inclined can make a &quot;Technocratic Union Facility&quot;), if it's in and of itself a powerful Wonder, or secret work of magick like Primium (then you also need to be powerful?, Archmastery even?), or what... </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Mastery of Primal Utility; and it's not unlike making a Device. Note that Primal Utility lets you make Devices one dot earlier than Prime lets you make Talismans, leaving Mastery with nothing special when it comes to Wonders. To the extent that Primal Utility remains exclusive to the Technocracy, so does the ability to set up these mass production facilities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whereas a rogue faction (like, say, Navalon) could be up the task...or maybe not even (the book specifies TU facilities...). </div> </div> </div>In the books as written, the idea of rogue factions hadn't really been explored. Certainly, at the time that <b>Book of Secrets</b> was written, the only mentions of anything resembling a faction of Enlightened Scientists that wasn't the Technocracy was a single line entry in <b>M20</b> indicating that the Harbingers of Avalon are on the verge of going rogue, and another single-line entry suggesting that one of the possible future members or allies of the Disparate Alliance might be Navalon. So the idea that only the Technocracy can do it may just be a reflection of the fact that the Technocracy had no competitors when this was written. <br /> <br /> (I'd also apply this concept to the Requisitions Background, which I see as being \u201cunique to the Technocracy\u201d because the Union has a surplus of Devices; and they <i>have</i> that surplus because they know the secret to mass production. If another faction were to unlock the secret to mass production, it would have the potential to build up its own warehouses of Devices, making Requisitions a possibility for them, too.)<br /> <br /> I'll note that <b>Rich Bastard's Guide to Magick</b> eliminated one monopoly that the Union had gained in the <b>Syndicate Convention Book</b> (i.e., access to Ventures); and the upcoming <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> has the Celestial Chorus develop an analog to Ventures (\u201cStable Wellsprings\u201d). So there's some precedent for breaking the Union's monopoly. I'm not inclined to completely break the \u201cmass production\u201d monopoly, at least not in this context; but I <i>could</i> see making it an \u201cEnlightened Science\u201d thing instead of a \u201cTechnocratic Union\u201d thing \u2014 bearing in mind that, barring the likes of Navalon and independent Enlightened Scientists, the Union is the only game in town. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morover, if Technocrats aren't using Will to alter reality...then they shouldn't be able to invest their Will on Devices when they're on their own. No?. It's either X or Y, not X when you don't care about it, but Y under durance. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And while I'm trying to keep house rules to a minimum, this might be a place where another house rule would be appropriate: namely, replace the expenditure of a dot of Willpower with a straight-up XP cost, based on what the Device rates as the Wonder Background. <br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to apply that across the board, instead of having it be a distinguishing factor between the Awakened and the Enlightened; while there's something flavorful about spending a dot of Willpower for crafting a Talisman, it has some drawbacks: the effective XP tax scales with your Willpower, not with the thing your making; meaning that the more Willpower you have, the more XP it will cost you to make Wonders without depleting your Willpower \u2014 and that this is true whether you're making a one-dot Wonder or a ten-dot Wonder. Switching it to an XP cost based on the Wonder rating fixes both of those problems. <br /> <br /> (Quick note: Willpower costs current rating \u00d7 1 to increase; and in mages, it will usually be at least 5. So this puts the XP tax for Wonders at 5\u201310 XP. Backgrounds, by contrast, cost current rating \u00d7 3 to purchase; so if we say that the XP cost for crafting a Wonder is the same as the XP cost for buying the Wonder Background, they can be horrendously expensive above two-dot Wonders. I'd be more inclined to go with a \u201crating\u00d72\u201d cost for this purpose.)<br /> <br /> Another thing that Willpower is used for, which Enlightened Scientists wouldn't be able to do, is to temporarily stave off the effects of Paradox. C'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-06-2022, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T10:28:35-07:00","id":1494457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494345#post1494345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Disclaimer: Long rant, and English is not my first language.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Can we be a bit more meta on the analysis? <br /> <br /> <br /> I am going to digress and complain a bit, but truly this is all because ignorant (although creative) writers started writing about things that they had no idea how work in real life. <br /> <br /> <br /> Most of the inconsistencies of the setting Magick vs Science is due to simply ignorant writers... That equal science with a &amp;quot;lack of soul&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;no poetry&amp;quot;... It was a bit cartoonish, and that is where most of the problems originated. <b>Consensus is an internally inconsistent idea, most of the setting is internally inconsistent, so we are discussing about things that not even current writers can fix, without unmaking the setting itself.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> True real world science is not machines or devices, it is a process, it is analyzing how the world works without preconceptions, what it is not what I want it to be. <b>A real world scientist would have already hypothesized that belief is what powers Traditions and would have found that this hypothesis fits all different paradigms</b>, and explains Marauders, Traditionalist, and Technocracy beliefs.<br /> <br /> <br /> From there,<b> the next question from a real world scientist would be WHY belief modifies the universe, not which beliefs should be held.</b> The WHY would give you true power over magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> The idea that Technocracy is winning because the masses believe in science, is... Dumb. Just plain dumb. Most of mankind is superstitious, religious in great deal, and/or completely ignorant how basic appliances work (let's not even talk about concepts like thermodynamics or special relativity). \u200bThe world should be more like a Cultivation novel, with plenty of magical beast, feudal lords, creatures... if the Consensus works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just to put some examples from other settings where bad writing makes the universe inconsistent, comic writers have Iron Man, a renowned industrialist, invent a portable communication device, lightweight materials, AND a portable high powered energy source... And the world is still the same! With just the technology necessary for the Iron Man suit (let's not even touch Reed Richards' tech, or Justice League tech in DC) any business consultant worth their salt would have changed the way computers, trains, cars, medical devices and life in general works.<br /> <br /> <br /> My comic example is to show how people trying to be &amp;quot;creative&amp;quot; but really not exploring the consequences of their hypothetical magic / technology, nor having any idea how a business work, or in the case of Mage the Ascension, not having any single clue how science works, at all, or not exploring the consequences of their ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>So all our threads and questions are going to be inconsistent because, to my great sorrow, the Mage the Ascension setting is poorly thought, badly designed, extremely inconsistent, and we are working upon almost 30 years of bad writing over a dumb start. We never are going to have good answers because the <i>setting</i> is just not good. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with you. Mage is my favorite game of all and not just for the D10, but Ive always know it is highly inconsistent. Vampire is inconsistent too, but Mage is even more. I just turn my suspension of disbelief 101% to play it, and leave the bigger philosophical questions out of the table because I know that if you delve too deep in it, it all falls apart.<br /> <br /> Ironically, I think the Techies work better if they are concious charlatans, as opposed to self deluded idiots, as in that they are fully aware that what they do is Magik, but disguise it in a bunch of technobabble on purpose to create a fake world they can control.<br /> <br /> But even then, the premisse is largely false: the vast majority of humanity do NOT believe in Quantum Physics and Molecular Sciences, because not even the scientists that research those fields know all about the others; a molecular biologist may have a superficial knowledge about Quantum Mechanics, but wont know all the equations of it, and vice versa. On the other hand thou, althought a good chunk of humanity loosely accepts the concepts of &quot;science&quot;, it is equally large the percentage that adheres to mysticism and spirituality - and even among scientists, the &quot;materialism&quot; which would be cornerstone philosophy of the Techies, is not an unanimous view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T10:59:46-07:00","id":1494459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494457#post1494457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically, I think the Techies work better if they are concious charlatans, as opposed to self deluded idiots, as in that they are fully aware that what they do is Magik, but disguise it in a bunch of technobabble on purpose to create a fake world they can control.</div> </div> </div> </div>If those were the only options, then I'd agree with you. But this thread is focused on a third possibility: that Enlightened Scientists are neither charlatans <i>nor</i> deluded idiots (or \u201cliars and dupes\u201d): that they <i>make a valid point</i>. In particular, I'm exploring the possibility that their claim that what they do (Enlightened Science) <i>is</i> distinct from what Superstitionists do (Awakened Magick) is true; it isn't \u201cmerely\u201d them stubbornly refusing to admit that they're wrong. <br /> <br /> And more importantly, as far as I'm concerned, you don't need to rely on the \u201ccontrol freaks/self-righteous busybodies\u201d aspect of the Technocracy in order to make sense of the pursuit of Enlightened Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-07-2022, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T16:35:27-07:00","id":1494561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494457#post1494457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even then, the premisse is largely false: the vast majority of humanity do NOT believe in Quantum Physics and Molecular Sciences, because not even the scientists that research those fields know all about the others; a molecular biologist may have a superficial knowledge about Quantum Mechanics, but wont know all the equations of it, and vice versa. On the other hand thou, althought a good chunk of humanity loosely accepts the concepts of &quot;science&quot;, it is equally large the percentage that adheres to mysticism and spirituality - and even among scientists, the &quot;materialism&quot; which would be cornerstone philosophy of the Techies, is not an unanimous view.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The vast majority of university graduates do not understand refrigerators... That cold is not an energy (the cold is <b>entering</b> the house!) but that is just lack of heat (the heat is <b>escaping</b> the house).<br /> <br /> Consensus should never, ever, work. Getting rid of it was one of the best things that Awakening did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494459#post1494459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those were the only options, then I'd agree with you. But this thread is focused on a third possibility: that Enlightened Scientists are neither charlatans <i>nor</i> deluded idiots (or \u201cliars and dupes\u201d): that they <i><b>make a valid point</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as per the game rules... They don't.<br /> <br /> It is the essence of the game that belief is what makes things work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494459#post1494459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, I'm exploring the possibility that their claim that what they do (Enlightened Science) <i>is</i> distinct from what Superstitionists do (Awakened Magick) is true; it isn't \u201cmerely\u201d them stubbornly refusing to admit that they're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is not distinct, again, just following games rules. That is why I put the example of what we do in day to day science, true scientific work. GROSSLY OVERSIMPLIFYING: we have ideas, we try to disprove them, if we fail to disprove we work based on those ideas until some compelling evidence to the contrary appears... This is my day job, I am telling you, science is not machines (that is technology), science is the process of how you do research, finding the principles that makes machines (technology) possible.<br /> <br /> So a <b>real</b> scientist (Enlightened or not) would ask WHY: Why only people that refer having an Avatar or Enlightened Genius can make these things work? Why strong belief on any type of explanation of how the universe works are perfectly correlated with deviant effects but also with Enlightened Science? Why does the Consensus works as it does? Why does Consensus exist in the first place? What it is enforcing it? Will it apply to sufficiently intelligent animals/creatures?<br /> <br /> Very unethically you could test that making people believe any nonsense (creating custom Deviants), or making them believe all known Enlightened Science EXCEPT certain already proven effect, if this person is unable to make it work it would give you evidence that their lack of belief is what makes the device fail. This elemental example is nowhere close to the complexity of what we do for a living... Now you tell me that recruited PhDs and lab experimenters, don't know how to do this because??? I am not even touching the extremely basic double blind protocols for testing things like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494459#post1494459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And more importantly, as far as I'm concerned, you don't need to rely on the \u201ccontrol freaks/self-righteous busybodies\u201d aspect of the Technocracy in order to make sense of the pursuit of Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the only way it makes sense given what I have explained in the previous paragraph, there is no way a halfway competent scientist would not even check the belief hypothesis UNLESS it is mandated from the upper echelons.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I dont know your professional background or you level of understanding how we do research, but the Technocratic processes <b>as described in the books,</b> are bad science, it is simply NOT done like this, anywhere that you have free, non-doctrine directed research (maybe on the 60's Soviet state commanded &quot;results&quot; or perhaps in China nowadays you would have it close to what books describe as the Technocracy science).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mage the Ascension is inconsistent, you can not find good explanations there because IT WAS WRITTEN BY IMAGINATIVE BUT IGNORANT PEOPLE, it will never be consistent from the starting premises.<br /> <br /> I like it, love the system for creating characters (merits and flaws for the color it give to a character), love that you can live the nerd fantasy that literal knowledge will make you a god among men.... But if you want to break a game like this, bring either a real life philosopher or chemist/physicist; your game will be derailed as long as you let them talk a few minutes, either the whole reality will no longer work as it should or you would have invincible combat monsters. <br /> <br /> When intellectual professionals apply themselves to this game, fun leaves through the window as you break it in moments, both at game and meta levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-07-2022, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T17:56:00-07:00","id":1494562,"title":"","content":"@Ibeaumanior: I'm not going to get into an argument with you about this. You see it as an intractable problem; I don't. And that's fine. But if your only contribution here is going to be to say that I'm being stupid by even trying, then you're not actually being constructive; you're just threadcrapping. So unless and until you post something constructive, I'm going to summarily ignore future posts from you without comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T18:59:05-07:00","id":1494565,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm still just scratching my head at the 'fix' your proposing. It makes sense from the Technocrat point of view...but <i>why</i> do the Traditions not recognize that they are different things? You can't claim that they just stubbornly cling to viewing everything from the lens of 'enlightened Will' because not every Tradition Mage is a Hermetic one. Hell, two of the Traditions are defectors <i>from</i> the Technocrat, what's the explanation for the Virtual Adepts and Sons of Ether? Are <i>they</i> using this alternative mechanism for doing their thing, or are they using the same thing as the rest of the Traditions? Did the Technocrats start out as Will workers and then find this new-fangled thing to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T19:42:23-07:00","id":1494567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494562#post1494562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ibeaumanior: I'm not going to get into an argument with you about this. You see it as an intractable problem; I don't. And that's fine. But if your only contribution here is going to be to say that I'm being stupid by even trying, then you're not actually being constructive; you're just threadcrapping. So unless and until you post something constructive, I'm going to summarily ignore future posts from you without comment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am arguing in good faith, that what you are trying to do, it is not possible, because it starts from false premises.<br /> <br /> <b>How is it not constructive to explain that you can not have a round triangle, and the why it is so?</b><br /> <br /> My triangle example is not a matter of who sees it as what, it is a matter of whether it is possible, I am arguing (perhaps not eloquently enough, but I have explained that this is not my main language) the reasons why it is not possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's say that the Enlightened Science is valid, how does it fit, in-game with other supers not being affected by the Consensus in the same way mages are? Where are the research lines on this? And the justification for ES validity, how does it explain the delusional reality deviants that are the Traditions? Why do the Traditions work in this framework? A theory has to explain or at least suggest what can fill its gaps. You should be able to make falsifiable predictions on it.<br /> <br /> The definition of &quot;Enlightened Science&quot; is more or less: science which is beyond the boundaries of the mainstream, but which at least pays lip-service to the scientific laws known and accepted by Sleeper scientists. I am explaining (quite at high level) what the basic most fundamental scientific laws are, research methods and understanding what science IS.<br /> <br /> This is like saying we have French Science and distinct but more effective British Science, such distinction does not exist. If right now we found out that the subatomic particles are all made of angel wings and fairy dust, we scientists would have to accept it <b>if that was the evidence</b>... There is no room for opinion when you have evidence (against or in favor of something).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More colloquially, you are free to try to do what you want, man... But I am trying to show why it does not make sense. For all their faults, <b>the game developers have put it clearly in the way the game works, the lore, the mechanics, that belief is what powers Magick</b>, Enlightened Science <b>in-game</b>, is as valid as praying to the rocks in your garden as long as you believe on it. <b>It is against the core premise of the game to make the ES paradigm special or different in any way (even its limitations on tool dependency are belief based).</b> The Ascension war is a war for mass belief, not that we Technos are right and Trad are wrong... Just that between competing frameworks of belief, which one will gain mass appeal. <i>It is written right there in the Core book, why are you discussing something that is settled as fundamental to the mechanics of how the system / game works? </i><br /> <br /> You might as well make a new game if you want science to have a specific validity... And that game where there are fundamental principles that get modified by how Magic works on top of it, it is called Mage the Awakening, it even has a whole group of mages looking for the interaction of technology and magic, because they understood that Science is analyzing how <i>everything</i> works (supernal magic, old plain physics, other supers abilities, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-07-2022, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T06:19:51-07:00","id":1494594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494459#post1494459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those were the only options, then I'd agree with you. But this thread is focused on a third possibility: that Enlightened Scientists are neither charlatans <i>nor</i> deluded idiots (or \u201cliars and dupes\u201d): that they <i>make a valid point</i>. In particular, I'm exploring the possibility that their claim that what they do (Enlightened Science) <i>is</i> distinct from what Superstitionists do (Awakened Magick) is true; it isn't \u201cmerely\u201d them stubbornly refusing to admit that they're wrong. <br /> <br /> And more importantly, as far as I'm concerned, you don't need to rely on the \u201ccontrol freaks/self-righteous busybodies\u201d aspect of the Technocracy in order to make sense of the pursuit of Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>The with this is: ok, Enlightened Science is real, and works based on the knowledge and the skills of the user, and the foundations of it are the natural laws of the universe, instead of the will of the operator.<br /> <br /> <br /> But how then do you explain Awakened Magik? Because clearly, Awakened Magik would represent a blatant violation of all the pillars around Enlightned Sciences are built upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T06:39:28-07:00","id":1494595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494567#post1494567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say that the Enlightened Science is valid, how does it fit, in-game with other supers not being affected by the Consensus in the same way mages are? Where are the research lines on this? And the justification for ES validity, how does it explain the delusional reality deviants that are the Traditions? Why do the Traditions work in this framework? A theory has to explain or at least suggest what can fill its gaps. You should be able to make falsifiable predictions on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I gave the idea of, let us call it this: &quot;Concious Quantum Fluctuations Applying the Butterfly Effect&quot; Theory, several replies above, upon which the very electrons of the &quot;mage's&quot; brain and every single molecules of his body create modifications at a quantum level that... Create a sort of chain effect that results in the &quot;magik&quot;. And this is done at a subconcious level. So it is will+external world, or rather, the &quot;will&quot; of anybody is actually a byproduct of the external superdeterministic universe, thus completely reversing the relation, since there isnt actually &quot;free will&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still, this is... REALLY pushing the line. It would be the ONLY explanation that materialism could accept to oppose full subjectivism, but if I were one of the &quot;Enlightned Scientists&quot; living the the MtA world, this would be such a strech that I would have to apply Occam's Razor and finally submit to the simpler explanation that yeah... perhaps it is, afterall, will that defines reality, in a subjective universe...<br /> <br /> Edit: oh yes, on your previous post you said something on the lines of &quot;how on Earth cant a &quot;common&quot; PhD use this &quot;Enlightned Science&quot;?&quot;. I fully agree. A molecular biologist PhD should be able to breed zerglings on tubes at a lab just as much as an &quot;Enlightned&quot; Primogenitor techie - if the premisse is that Enlightned Science is indeed based on natural principles as opposed to outright &quot;miracle workings&quot;.<br /> <br /> On a note, I play Mage the Ascension using GURPS system - there is a Gurps: Mage the Ascension book for Gurps 3e, but I modified it for the 4e of Gurps, and expanded it a lot; for instance, my games dont have the 9 Spheres alone, each magical group have their own Spheres and systems, and it's all balanced due to the Gurps model of using character points for everything. So, my Dreamspeakers have 3 Spheres only, there are also &quot;sub spheres&quot; like &quot;Telekinesis Sphere&quot; or &quot;Pyromancy Sphere&quot;, or &quot;Plant Sphere&quot;, and as many as you'd wish (I have &quot;Necromancy&quot;, &quot;Alchemy&quot;, &quot;Fire Elemental&quot; and many others as &quot;sub spheres&quot;), and it's all balanced by point costs.<br /> <br /> Gurps has an interesting Advantage called &quot;Gadgeteer&quot;; it's basically what Tony Stark, Bruce Wayne or Macguyver have, the ability to build strange gadgets using potatoes, some wires and an old car battery. I have been thinking on using THAT as the base for my Techie boys for my games, as opposed to an &quot;Awakened Avatar&quot;.<br /> <br /> Therefore, in my games, the Techies will indeed be geniuses scientists, that work entirely inside the realm of natural laws.<br /> Mages on the other hand are willworkers that perform &quot;miracles&quot; - at the latin root of the world, &quot;do the impossible&quot;. So, &quot;Magik&quot; actively BREAKS the natural order, and is something that goes beyond the natural world.<br /> <br /> For my games, and in Gurps rules, there's also rules for exchanging money for character points, therefore all the Gadgets have a money cost based on character points for the equivalent advantage - for instance, a &quot;quantum insubstantiator&quot; to turn you &quot;insubstantial&quot; is equivalent to a 80 points advantage, therefore it costs 80 x (base value per point) thousands of dollars to be created. This way, this system have it's own internal balance too, and I found that it greatly improves the setting - giving a much more significant importance to the Syndicate, for example, since the Union is as powerful now as their pockets allows it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 10-08-2022, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T22:22:30-07:00","id":1494656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494594#post1494594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The with this is: ok, Enlightened Science is real, and works based on the knowledge and the skills of the user, and the foundations of it are the natural laws of the universe, instead of the will of the operator.<br /> <br /> <br /> But how then do you explain Awakened Magik? Because clearly, Awakened Magik would represent a blatant violation of all the pillars around Enlightned Sciences are built upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is that Awakened Magick isn't Enlightened Science. The Technocracy claims that what the Superstitionists do isn't what the Technocracy does; so why would you have to explain how Awakened Magick works within the context of Enlightened Science?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T09:22:48-07:00","id":1494680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494656#post1494656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is that Awakened Magick isn't Enlightened Science. The Technocracy claims that what the Superstitionists do isn't what the Technocracy does; so why would you have to explain how Awakened Magick works within the context of Enlightened Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with the entire &quot;SCP&quot; Foundation, which is a series of horror story's fictional creatures created on the internet?<br /> <br /> SCP standing for &quot;Search, Contain, Protect&quot;, and it's a giant compilation of lovecraftian-easc beings of all kinds, where the weirdness of them is perhaps the main factor.<br /> <br /> It has a sort of &quot;X-Files&quot; to it. The SCP Foundation also have a sort of &quot;Technocratic Union&quot; or &quot;Men in Black&quot; vibe to it.<br /> <br /> I had seen those a long time ago, and had forgot about it. After this post however, I &quot;freudian slip&quot; back into it, and watched a few YT videos.<br /> <br /> So, each monster (sometimes it's not a creature, but a weird occurence or object) has an SCP designation. For example, SCP 682 is the &quot;undestructable lizard&quot;, a giant lizard filled with hate that kills everything he sees and has almost limitless regeneration and adaptation. SCP 096 is an undestructable humanoid that kills anyone that sees his face. SCP 073 is Abel, and SCP 076 is Cain. Yes, from the Bible.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the Foundation studies and contain the mysterious threats out there, and protect humanity in secret, sort like the MiB or the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> After thinking about it... I found it to be a fascinating concept. And something similar could work for MtA.<br /> <br /> But there would have to be some modifications to the premisses of the game. First of all, the full on hardcore 100% subjectivity of the world. I guess it would be better that, like you said, Enlightned Science works within the boundaries of the natural world - ie REAL SCIENCE. And Magik would become a real &quot;Miracle Work&quot;, aka &quot;Magik&quot; defies or break the natural laws. <br /> <br /> Thus, &quot;Mages&quot; truly are REALITY DEVIANTS in a much more literal sense.<br /> <br /> And, the Techies job is more akin to that of the internet creepypasta &quot;Foundation&quot;; to deal with all the weird shit reality deviants out there, like Mages that break reality, bloodsucking vampires, metamorphic beasts and tentacle monsters from beyond the void. The job is to study those if possible, destroy them if safer and contain those abominations if there's no other way.<br /> <br /> The Union however is not all wise about all those mysteries however; there would be some theories, some amount of knowledge, particularly about how to hunt, contain and/or destroy those things, but not much about the true nature of any of that, because those things simply defy conventional science, sometimes even outright contradict it, and some are not even just unkown threats, but <i>unkowable</i>.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, the Techies know that those &quot;Mages&quot; talk about &quot;Avatars&quot; and what not, but whatever that is (if even true), it is absolutely elusive to the Union.<br /> <br /> Hell, in such a setting some &quot;Mages&quot; may even work for the Union, under a never ending constant surveillance from agents, but you could have a &quot;Warlock&quot; summoning spiritual bats to help a ciborg fight an insane Infernalist summoning imps from hell.<br /> <br /> This do become a very different game thou, but I recon it would be hell of fun too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T09:41:33-07:00","id":1494681,"title":"","content":"With those changes, it would be perfectly fine to have a &quot;Shaman&quot; working helping the Union, or a &quot;Druid&quot; (aka Verbena or whatever similar), doing literally MAGIK that the Agents dont understand (and shit their pants about) to hunt down demons, dimensional beasts and etc. And, even when those special &quot;Mage Agents&quot; talk about &quot;Awakening&quot;, &quot;Avatar&quot; or whatever, the Union's scientists take notes, smile and nod, and whisper amongst themselves about &quot;what a bunch of nonsense&quot;.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Rogue Enlightned Scientists - aka Etherites and VAs - have defected and now work for this other conspiracy of the Reality Deviants that they themselves call &quot;Traditions&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, something like the Bureau of... Paranormal Activities? I dont exactly recall if that's the name, but it's the FBI-like agency that does this job in the Hellboy comics universe. So, for example, they have Hellboy working for them, helping humanity, and a few other monsters too.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the SCP Foundation also has a few of the monsters helping them. For example, SCP 073, Cain (sorry, is the biblical character, brother of Abel, is his name Cain, Caine or Caim in english? Im not sure). Well, this SCP is very helpfull, very wise. He basically is one of the most important agents of the Foundation, he has basically full freedom of access and movement inside it, and is a huge source of knowledge for the Foundation. SCP 999 is another example of helpful SCP creature, and likewise has a huge amount of freedom; in fact, SCP 999 is universally loved inside the Foundation, since it has the ability to make anybody happy.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the Union could have something similar. &quot;Friendly vampires&quot;, for example, or more rarely even shapeshifters, working for them, having a big amount of freedom within certain controlled boundaries inside the Union and having certain amounts of ammenities and even luxuries - all of that depending on their behavior and amount of help that those provide to the mission. The same being true about Mages.<br /> <br /> Also, those creatures that are too &quot;unruly&quot; and/or &quot;uncooperative&quot;, would either be in a cage, drugged and constantly experimented on in labs, or outright destructed (or &quot;banned&quot; to... some other plane, if no other option).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T13:21:33-07:00","id":1494695,"title":"","content":"Personally, I repurpose the Syndicate's Special Projects Division for SCP Foundation type stuff. That is, my version of SPD isn't <i>just</i> or even <i>primarily</i> about Pentex; it likely has connections to vampiric society, to Orpheus, even to the occasional changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-09T13:46:50-07:00","id":1494696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494680#post1494680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there would have to be some modifications to the premisses of the game. First of all, the full on hardcore 100% subjectivity of the world. I guess it would be better that, like you said, Enlightned Science works within the boundaries of the natural world - ie REAL SCIENCE. And Magik would become a real &quot;Miracle Work&quot;, aka &quot;Magik&quot; defies or break the natural laws.<br /> <br /> Thus, &quot;Mages&quot; truly are REALITY DEVIANTS in a much more literal sense.<br /> <br /> And, the Techies job is more akin to that of the internet creepypasta &quot;Foundation&quot;; to deal with all the weird shit reality deviants out there, like Mages that break reality, bloodsucking vampires, metamorphic beasts and tentacle monsters from beyond the void. The job is to study those if possible, destroy them if safer and contain those abominations if there's no other way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to look into the game &quot;Unknown Armies&quot;, not to dwell much on it, but there are broadly 3 types of magic: Avatar magic (you copy one of the existing archetypes, or try to become one), adepts (who have such particular obsessions that they alter reality, you HAVE to be insane to do adept magic) and rituals (in general less powerful, but repeatable and doesnt require you to be mad to function).<br /> <br /> <br /> So any deviant would be an Adept, a technomancer will be closer to a Ritualist (the rituals are very weird, some are hermetic, some are postmodern, but they are in a sense part of reality and WILL work, just hard to do)....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T07:25:09-07:00","id":1494863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492820-on-science-and-magick?p=1494656#post1494656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is that Awakened Magick isn't Enlightened Science. The Technocracy claims that what the Superstitionists do isn't what the Technocracy does; so why would you have to explain how Awakened Magick works within the context of Enlightened Science?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Between the Etherites and VAs defecting, the brainwashing of Traditionalists, and the occational Nephandic infiltration there is quite a bit of reason for Technocrats to at least explore the idea. I'd say there probably is a complicated Technocratic explanation for how reality deviancy fits in with enlightened science, but we don't really know the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T21:22:29-07:00","id":1494907,"title":"","content":"One side effect of putting expertise front and center is that you quickly discover that no one can be an expert on everything. That said, different people can be experts in different things. What this means is that no particular Enlightened Scientist knows everything; but the answer to any particular question can probably be found if you talk to the right person. <br /> <br /> In the case of the relationship between Awakened Magick and Enlightened Science, this means that the average Technocrat doesn't have an answer; but he knows that there are experts in the Union who <i>do</i> know; and that's good enough for him, because he has his <i>own</i> area of expertise to think about. And the experts on how Awakened Magick and Enlightened Science relate to each other are the folks in the Special Projects Division: <i>they're</i> the guys tasked with studying supernatural phenomena and turning it into useful technology. If anyone in the Union would have a precise answer to the question of just what differentiates the two, SPD would. <br /> <br /> As I speculated earlier, I think the answer lies in the distinction between Avatar and Genius: the Traditions see those as merely different names for the same thing, while the TU's experts on the matter see them as similar, but fundamentally different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-12T22:39:02-07:00","id":1494908,"title":"","content":"...that doesn't really address Ramnesis's point though? If the VA and Etherites are still defectors from the Technocracy, in this new paradigm, are they using an Avatar or Genius? How does Room 101 work in this version of Mage? CAN room 101 still work in this version of the lore, or are Technocrats and Traditionalists 'locked' into their faction, because of incompatible underlying mechanics?<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry, just realised that this came across a bit strongly, no offence was intended here, but just curious about what your thoughts are in regards to Room 101 and the defection of the VA and Etherites./","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","user":"Furoan","date":". 10-13-2022, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T05:13:11-07:00","id":1494917,"title":"","content":"Yes, Room 101 can still work in this framework; in some ways, it's <i>essential</i>. Mind you, the NWO goes overboard with Conditioning, taking it beyond its core function and turning it into a tool to impose conformity. They also apply it to the unwilling, which isn't good. But at its core, what Conditioning is all about is converting an Avatar into Genius. You go in a Mage and come out a Scientist. (Note that the Void Engineers practice a more lax form of Conditioning; enough to transition Avatar to Genius, but mostly lacking the conformal indoctrination of Room 101. I would also apply this to the Syndicate's Special Projects Division, and to the Harbingers of Avalon, who specialize in <i>breaking</i> Conditioning.) <br /> <br /> The advantage of this is that it explains why Genius doesn't cover the same range of possibilities that an Avatar does: Genius is almost always Circumspect (house rule: make Circumspect Avatar a \u201c0-point Merit\u201d) and never Manifest (which means that you cannot take your Genius as an Ally, Familiar, Spirit Mentor, or anything else that implies that it's a separate entity and not just part of your personality); in fact, <i>most</i> Supernatural Merits and Flaws are incompatible with Enlightenment without creative reinterpretation; it would probably be easier to list the ones that <i>are</i> compatible than to list the ones that <i>aren't</i>. Awakened Magi with Supernatural Merits and Flaws that are incompatible with Enlightened Science either can't be converted at all, or are harder to convert and lose the incompatible traits in the transition. For instance, a former Mage with a Manifest Avatar will never see his \u201cimaginary friend\u201d again after conversion, outside of an Epiphany (though chances are good that he'll develop the Demented Eidolon Flaw); but if the Mage with the Manifest Avatar went so far as to take his Avatar as an Ally, and/or has the Phylactery Flaw, his Avatar cannot become Genius. If Avatar-to-Genius is impossible but the \u201cconversion\u201d is otherwise successful, the former mage still loses the incompatible traits, <i>and</i> loses her Arete <i>without</i> replacing it with Enlightenment, becoming an Extraordinary Citizen. That's not necessarily as big of a problem as it might seem at first; as I see it, the vast majority of Technocrats are Extraordinary Citizens, and the Enlightened Scientists are the elite few who find it exceptionally easy to innovate. <br /> <br /> The Traditions view this transition from Avatar to Genius as being \u201cmerely\u201d a shift in Focus, albeit a more extreme one than even the difference between mystics and technomancers; and the least gracious among them compare it to how a Caul \u201cinverts\u201d an Avatar. That is, they tend to consider a Genius to be a suppressed Avatar. By contrast, the Technocracy views technomancy as an Avatar emulating Genius: mages pretending to be scientists. Enlightened Scientists view this as the \u201cworst of both worlds\u201d: the technomancer is nearly as dependent on tools and techniques as the Enlightened Scientist is, <i>and</i> labors under the restrictions of Willworking, and thus gets the full benefits of neither. Technomancers who consider such things, meanwhile, view themselves as a bridge between Enlightened Scientists and Awakened Mystics. <br /> <br /> The defectors from the Union were still Enlightened Scientists when they defected. Their recruits, on the other hand, are mostly technomancers; and \u201creverse Conditioning\u201d (from Genius to Avatar) <i>is</i> a thing; so someone who starts out with Enlightenment can undergo a process to become a technomancer. So these days, the Etherites and Virtual Adepts are mostly Awakened Technomancers rather than Enlightened Scientists \u2014 though the Etherites still call themselves true Scientists and say that Technocrats <i>aren't</i> Scientists. And with the rise of the Mercurial Elite, there's now a movement within the VAs to abandon even technomancy and go full-on mystic (though given their origins, the Mercurial Elite have a disproportionate number of Techgnosi in their ranks). That said, you can still find the occasional Enlightened Scientist in the ranks of these organizations. <br /> <br /> Navalon, on the other hand, probably still practices a more benign version of Conditioning, more akin to a Void Engineer's Conditioning than to Room 101: there's some basic education to ensure that the recruit has the overall mindset of a Scientist, but only what's necessary to allow the transition from Avatar and Arete to Genius and Enlightenment. For now, at least, the group is making efforts to remain a faction of Enlightened Scientists and to avoid drifting into Willworking the way the Etherites and VAs did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-13-2022, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-13T20:43:53-07:00","id":1494956,"title":"","content":"I have updated the original post to include some of this last post. My latest thought on the matter: I think that Technocrats would argue that mages have Avatars but that Enlightened Scientists achieve similar results without one, relying instead on an innate human capacity for innovation (the quality of Genius that's actualized as Enlightenment) that an Avatar usurps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T07:40:51-07:00","id":1494968,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I really think that one starts pushing down the path of Technocrats being deliberately blind or stupid. <br /> <br /> I would suggest this alternative: The Technocracy's position is that Avatars are a distorted form of natural human capacity. They would argue that Traditionalists have either anthropomorphized their innate abilities or allowed some external entity to hijack them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T09:15:13-07:00","id":1494972,"title":"","content":"The \u201cexternal entity hijacks their innate abilities\u201d is essentially what I was going for (although less antagonistic Enlightened Scientists who know of such things would probably use a less abrasive term than \u201chijack\u201d). This could also be tied into the \u201cpsychopomps joining Avatars to human souls\u201d bit that MRev introduced. <br /> <br /> I would reserve the \u201canthropomorphized innate abilities\u201d explanation for the rare Enlightened Scientist who hears voices in his head.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea is that \u201cGenius/Enlightenment/Innovation\u201d is the innate human ability in its purest form, while \u201cAvatar/Arete/Willworking\u201d is what you get when an external entity takes charge of that innate human ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-14-2022, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:40:41-07:00","id":1495112,"title":"","content":"The way some Technocrats have voices in their head is the exact reason I suggested &quot;anthropomorphized innate abilities.&quot; Since they are familiar with the phenomenon they would certainly apply the explanation to Traditionalists as well. <br /> <br /> I think it is a good idea to give them a range of explanations for Avatars so they aren't disconcerted when one doesn't behave in normal parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}